registerFaith({code:'ne',
stories:[
{id:'fstory',title:'God’s Story',ne:'परमेश्वरको कथा',
overview:{t:'The whole story in short',ne:'सुसमाचार — छोटकरीमा',art:FNE_ART.ovstory,
start:['सुरुदेखि हेरौं','From here — the whole story in detail'],
paras:[
['सुरुमा परमेश्वरले पृथ्वी र त्यसमा भएका सबै थोक बनाउनुभयो। अनि उहाँले मानिसलाई आफ्नै स्वरूपमा बनाउनुभयो — सम्बन्धको लागि, प्रेमको लागि।','Surumaa Parameshwarle prithvi ra tyasmaa bhaekaa sabai thok banaunubhayo. Ani uhaanle maanislaai aaphnai swaroopmaa banaunubhayo — sambandhako laagi, premko laagi.','In the beginning God created the earth and everything in it. And he made human beings in his own image — for relationship, for love.','Genesis 1:26–27'],
['मानिस र परमेश्वरको बीचमा मित्रता थियो। तर मानिसले परमेश्वरको विरुद्धमा विद्रोह गर्ने बाटो रोज्यो — र त्यही विद्रोहले हामीलाई परमेश्वरबाट अलग गर्यो।','Maanis ra Parameshwarko beechmaa mitrataa thiyo. Tara maanisle Parameshwarko biruddhamaa vidroha garne baato rojyo — ra tyahi vidrohale haamilaai Parameshwarbaata alag garyo.','Humanity and God shared friendship. But human beings chose the road of rebellion against God — and that rebellion separated us from him.','Genesis 3'],
['विद्रोह रोज्ने त हामी नै थियौं — तैपनि परमेश्वरले हामीलाई यति प्रेम गर्नुभयो कि उहाँले त्यो भाँचिएको सम्बन्ध निको पारेर फेरि जोड्ने योजना बनाउनुभयो।','Vidroha rojne ta haami nai thiyaun — taipani Parameshwarle haamilaai yati prem garnubhayo ki uhaanle tyo bhaanchieko sambandha niko paarera pheri jodne yojanaa banaunubhayo.','We were the ones who chose to rebel — yet God loved us so much that he made a plan to heal that broken relationship and join it back together.','Genesis 3:15'],
['त्यसैले परमेश्वरले एउटा जाति छान्नुभयो — इस्राएल। अब्राहाम नाम गरेका एक जना साधारण मानिसबाट सुरु भएको त्यो जातिलाई उहाँले प्रतिज्ञा दिनुभयो — तिमीहरूद्वारा संसारका सबै जातिले आशिष् पाउनेछन्। त्यही जातिद्वारा उहाँले सारा संसारमा निको पार्ने काम र मुक्ति ल्याउनुहुनेथियो।','Tyasaile Parameshwarle eutaa jaati chhaannubhayo — Israel. Abrahaam naam garekaa ek janaa saadhaaran maanisbaata suru bhaeko tyo jaatilaai uhaanle pratigyaa dinubhayo — timiharudwaaraa sansaarkaa sabai jaatile aashish paaunechhan. Tyahi jaatidwaaraa uhaanle saaraa sansaarmaa niko paarne kaam ra mukti lyaunuhunethiyo.','So God chose one nation — Israel. It began with a single ordinary man named Abraham, and God promised him: through you, all the peoples of the earth will be blessed. Through this nation God would bring healing and salvation to the whole world.','Genesis 12:1–3'],
['किनभने सयौं वर्षपछि, त्यही जातिबाट, येशू आउनुभयो। उहाँ कन्याबाट जन्मनुभयो; उहाँ परमेश्वरका पुत्र हुनुहुन्छ। उहाँ हामीलाई हाम्रो विद्रोहबाट बचाउन र परमेश्वरसँगको हाम्रो सम्बन्ध निको पार्न आउनुभयो।','Kinabhane sayaun barshapachhi, tyahi jaatibaata, Yeshu aaunubhayo. Uhaan kanyaabaata janmanubhayo; uhaan Parameshwarkaa putra hunuhunchha. Uhaan haamilaai haamro vidrohabaata bachaauna ra Parameshwarsangako haamro sambandha niko paarna aaunubhayo.','Because hundreds of years later, from that very nation, Jesus came. He was born of a virgin; he is the Son of God. He came to save us from our rebellion and to heal our relationship with God.','Matthew 1:18–23 · Luke 19:10'],
['यो यसरी भयो — येशू हाम्रा पापको लागि बलिको रूपमा क्रूसमा मर्नुभयो। अनि तेस्रो दिन उहाँ मृत्युबाट जीवित हुनुभयो — जुन अन्धकारमा हामी मानिसहरू फसेका थियौं, त्यसैलाई उहाँले जित्नुभयो।','Yo yasari bhayo — Yeshu haamraa paapko laagi baliko rupmaa kroosmaa marnubhayo. Ani tesro din uhaan mrityubaata jeewit hunubhayo — jun andhakaarmaa haami maanisharu phasekaa thiyaun, tyasailaai uhaanle jitnubhayo.','It happened like this: Jesus died on the cross as the sacrifice for our sins. And on the third day he rose from the dead — overcoming the very darkness we humans were trapped in.','1 Corinthians 15:3–4'],
['आज येशू जीवित हुनुहुन्छ र परमेश्वरको दाहिने हातपट्टि हुनुहुन्छ। जसले उहाँमाथि विश्वास गरेर उहाँलाई पछ्याउँछ, त्यो परमेश्वरको परिवारमा फर्काइन्छ — परमेश्वरकै सन्तान भएर।','Aaja Yeshu jeewit hunuhunchha ra Parameshwarko daahine haatpatti hunuhunchha. Jasle uhaanmaathi vishwaas garera uhaanlaai pachhyaunchha, tyo Parameshwarko pariwaarmaa pharkaainchha — Parameshwarkai santaan bhaera.','Today Jesus is alive, seated at the right hand of God. And whoever believes in him and follows him is brought home into God’s family — as God’s own child.','Hebrews 12:2 · John 1:12'],
['विश्वास गर्नेहरूलाई परमेश्वरले आफ्नो पवित्र आत्मा दिनुहुन्छ — परमेश्वर आफैँ हामीभित्र बास गर्नुहुन्छ, सान्त्वना दिनुहुन्छ र दिनदिनै बाटो देखाउनुहुन्छ।','Vishwaas garneharulaai Parameshwarle aaphno Pawitra Aatmaa dinuhunchha — Parameshwar aaphain haamibhitra baas garnuhunchha, saantwanaa dinuhunchha ra dindinai baato dekhaunuhunchha.','To those who believe, God gives his Holy Spirit — God himself making his home within us, comforting us and guiding us day by day.','John 14:16–17'],
['र एक दिन येशू फेरि आउनुहुनेछ। उहाँले सबै थोक नयाँ बनाउनुहुनेछ — न आँसु, न मृत्यु — र परमेश्वर आफ्ना मानिसहरूसँग सधैँको लागि बास गर्नुहुनेछ।','Ra ek din Yeshu pheri aaunuhunechha. Uhaanle sabai thok nayaan banaunuhunechha — na aansu, na mrityu — ra Parameshwar aaphnaa maanisharusanga sadhainko laagi baas garnuhunechha.','And one day Jesus will come again. He will make all things new — no more tears, no more death — and God will dwell with his people forever.','Revelation 21:1–4'],
['यही सन्देशले विश्वास गर्ने हरेकलाई निको पार्छ र फेरि जोड्छ — हाम्रो र परमेश्वरको बीचको सङ्गति फर्काइदिन्छ। यही नै सुसमाचार हो — हामीले कमाएको होइन, परमेश्वरले दिनुभएको उपहार।','Yahi sandeshle vishwaas garne hareklaai niko paarchha ra pheri jodchha — haamro ra Parameshwarko beechko sangati pharkaaidinchha. Yahi nai susamaachaar ho — haamile kamaaeko hoina, Parameshwarle dinubhaeko upahaar.','This message brings healing and restoration to everyone who believes it — it gives back the fellowship between us and God. This is the gospel: not something we earn, but a gift God gives.','Romans 1:16 · Ephesians 2:8–9'],
['यो मानिसजातिको लागि परमेश्वरको योजना र उहाँले सारा संसारमा कसरी मुक्ति ल्याउनुभयो भन्ने कुराको सार हो। अब यहाँबाट हामी यही कथा सुरुदेखि, एक-एक घटना गरेर, विस्तारमा हेर्नेछौं।','Yo maanisjaatiko laagi Parameshwarko yojanaa ra uhaanle saaraa sansaarmaa kasari mukti lyaaunubhayo bhanne kuraako saar ho. Aba yahaanbaata haami yahi kathaa surudekhi, ek-ek ghatanaa garera, vistaarmaa hernechhaun.','This is an overview of God’s plan for humanity, and how he brought salvation to the whole world. From here, we will walk through the same story from the beginning — one moment at a time, in detail.']]},
sections:[
{id:'creation',t:'In the beginning',ne:'सुरुमा',art:FNE_ART.creation,
note:['परमेश्वरलाई हाम्रो खाँचो थिएन — उहाँले हामीलाई चाहनुभयो। मानिस उहाँसँगको मित्रताको लागि बनाइएको हो, र कथा त्यो मित्रता पूर्ण भएको असल संसारबाट सुरु हुन्छ।','Parameshwarlaai haamro khaancho thiena — uhaanle haamilaai chaahanubhayo. Maanis uhaansangako mitrataako laagi banaieko ho, ra kathaa tyo mitrataa purna bhaeko asal sansaarbaata suru hunchha.','God did not need us — he wanted us. Human beings were made for friendship with their Maker, and the story opens in a good world where that friendship is whole.'],
paras:[
['सुरुमा परमेश्वरले आकाश र पृथ्वी बनाउनुभयो। सबै कुरा असल थियो।','Surumaa Parameshwarle aakaash ra prithvi banaunubhayo. Sabai kuraa asal thiyo.','In the beginning God made the heavens and the earth. Everything he made was good.','Genesis 1'],
['परमेश्वरले मानिसलाई आफ्नै स्वरूपमा बनाउनुभयो — पुरुष र स्त्री।','Parameshwarle maanislaai aaphnai swaroopmaa banaunubhayo — purush ra stree.','God made human beings in his own image — male and female.','Genesis 1:27'],
['स्वरूपमा बनाइनुको अर्थ गहिरो थियो — हामीले परमेश्वरको चरित्र र स्वभाव सारा सृष्टिको सामु झल्काउनुपर्थ्यो। बाँकी सृष्टिभन्दा फरक, मानिस उहाँकै प्रतिबिम्ब हुन बनाइएको थियो।','Swaroopmaa banaainuko artha gahiro thiyo — haamile Parameshwarko charitra ra swabhaaw saaraa srishtiko saamu jhalkaunuparthyo. Baanki srishtibhandaa pharak, maanis uhaankai pratibimba huna banaaieko thiyo.','And being made in his image meant something deep: humans were to reflect the character and nature of God to the whole creation. Unlike the rest of what he made, we were made to be his likeness.','Genesis 1:26–28'],
['परमेश्वरले मानिसलाई भन्नुभयो — फल्दै-फुल्दै जाओ, र यस पृथ्वीको हेरचाह गर। काम पनि आशिष् थियो।','Parameshwarle maanislaai bhannubhayo — phaldai-phuldai jaao, ra yas prithviko herchaah gara. Kaam pani aashish thiyo.','God told the humans: be fruitful, and take care of this earth. Even work was a blessing.','Genesis 1:28 · 2:15'],
['अदन नाम गरेको एउटा बगैंचामा मानिसहरू परमेश्वरसँगै बस्थे। उहाँ तिनीहरूसँग त्यहीँ हिँड्नुहुन्थ्यो — मानिस र परमेश्वरको बीचमा अटुट सम्बन्ध, मीठो सङ्गति थियो।','Adan naam gareko eutaa bagainchaamaa maanisharu Parameshwarsangai basthe. Uhaan tiniharusanga tyahin hindnuhunthyo — maanis ra Parameshwarko beechmaa atut sambandha, meetho sangati thiyo.','The humans dwelt with God in a garden called Eden. He would walk with them there — an unbroken relationship, sweet fellowship between humanity and God.','Genesis 2:8 · 3:8'],
['बगैंचाको बीचमा एउटा रूख थियो। परमेश्वरले भन्नुभयो — त्यसको फल नखाओ; खायौ भने तिमी मर्नेछौ। किनभने प्रेम गर्नुहुने परमेश्वरले हामीलाई सधैँ रोज्ने ठाउँ दिनुहुन्छ — उहाँसँगको सम्बन्ध चाहन्छौं कि चाहँदैनौं, त्यो हामीले नै रोज्नुपर्छ।','Bagainchaako beechmaa eutaa rukh thiyo. Parameshwarle bhannubhayo — tyasko phal nakhaao; khaayau bhane timi marnechhau. Kinabhane prem garnuhune Parameshwarle haamilaai sadhain rojne thaaun dinuhunchha — uhaansangako sambandha chaahanchhaun ki chaahandainaun, tyo haamile nai rojnuparchha.','In the middle of the garden stood one tree, and God said: do not eat its fruit — if you eat it, you will die. Because the God who loves always leaves us a choice: do we want relationship with him, or not? That choice is ours to make.','Genesis 2:16–17'],
['परमेश्वरले आफ्नो सबै कामलाई हेर्नुभयो र भन्नुभयो — धेरै असल छ। अनि सातौं दिनमा उहाँले विश्राम गर्नुभयो।','Parameshwarle aaphno sabai kaamlaai hernubhayo ra bhannubhayo — dherai asal chha. Ani saataun dinmaa uhaanle vishraam garnubhayo.','God looked at all he had made and said: it is very good. And on the seventh day he rested.','Genesis 1:31 · 2:2–3']]},
{id:'fall',t:'The break',ne:'सङ्गति भाँचियो',art:FNE_ART.fall,
note:['पापको जरा नियम तोड्नु मात्र होइन — परमेश्वरमाथिको भरोसा तोड्नु हो। तैपनि सबैभन्दा अँध्यारो पानामा पनि परमेश्वरले उद्धारकको प्रतिज्ञा दिइसक्नुभएको छ।','Paapko jaraa niyam todnu maatra hoina — Parameshwarmaathiko bharosaa todnu ho. Taipani sabaibhandaa andhyaaro paanaamaa pani Parameshwarle uddhaarakko pratigyaa diisaknubhaeko chha.','The root of sin is not rule-breaking but trust-breaking. Yet even on the darkest page, God has already promised a Rescuer.'],
paras:[
['ती पहिला मानिसहरूका नाम आदम र हव्वा थिए। तर त्यो असल बगैंचामा एक दिन एउटा सर्प आयो — र त्यसले झूट बोल्यो। दुःखको कुरा, आदम र हव्वाले परमेश्वरको वचन छोडेर सर्पकै कुरामा विश्वास गरे — र तिनीहरूले त्यो फल खाए।','Ti pahilaa maanisharukaa naam Aadam ra Hawwaa thie. Tara tyo asal bagainchaamaa ek din eutaa sarpa aayo — ra tyasle jhoot bolyo. Dukhako kuraa, Aadam ra Hawwaale Parameshwarko wachan chhodera sarpakai kuraamaa vishwaas gare — ra tiniharule tyo phal khaae.','The names of those first humans were Adam and Eve. But one day, into that good garden, came a serpent — and it told a lie. Sadly, Adam and Eve let go of God’s word and believed the snake instead — and they ate the fruit.','Genesis 3:1–6'],
['सर्पको झूट यस्तो थियो — यो फल खायौ भने तिमीहरू परमेश्वरजस्तै हुनेछौ। परमेश्वरलाई भरोसा गर्न सकिँदैन; उहाँले तिमीहरूबाट असल कुरा लुकाउँदै हुनुहुन्छ।','Sarpako jhoot yasto thiyo — yo phal khaayau bhane timiharu Parameshwarjastai hunechhau. Parameshwarlaai bharosaa garna sakindaina; uhaanle timiharubaata asal kuraa lukaaundai hunuhunchha.','The lie went like this: eat this fruit, and you will become like God. God cannot be trusted — he is withholding good things from you.','Genesis 3:4–5'],
['फल खानेबित्तिकै तिनीहरूको हृदय दोष र लाजले भरियो — र तिनीहरू लुके। पहिलो पटक मानिस परमेश्वरदेखि डरायो।','Phal khaanebittikai tiniharuko hridaya dosh ra laajle bhariyo — ra tiniharu luke. Pahilo patak maanis Parameshwardekhi daraayo.','The moment they ate, guilt and shame flooded their hearts — and they hid. For the first time, humans were afraid of God.','Genesis 3:7–10'],
['तैपनि परमेश्वरले तिनीहरूलाई खोज्दै आउनुभयो र सोध्नुभयो — तिमी कहाँ छौ? अनि उहाँले आफ्नै हातले तिनीहरूलाई लुगा लगाइदिनुभयो।','Taipani Parameshwarle tiniharulaai khojdai aaunubhayo ra sodhnubhayo — timi kahaan chhau? Ani uhaanle aaphnai haatle tiniharulaai lugaa lagaaidinubhayo.','Yet God came looking for them and asked: where are you? And with his own hands he clothed them.','Genesis 3:9 · 3:21'],
['जब परमेश्वरले सोध्नुभयो, आदमले हव्वालाई दोष दिए, र हव्वाले सर्पलाई। पापले हामीलाई एकअर्काबाट पनि टाढा बनाउँछ।','Jaba Parameshwarle sodhnubhayo, Aadamle Hawwaalaai dosh die, ra Hawwaale sarpalaai. Paaple haamilaai ekarkaabaata pani taadhaa banaunchha.','When God asked what had happened, Adam blamed Eve, and Eve blamed the serpent. Sin pushes us apart from one another too.','Genesis 3:12–13'],
['परमेश्वरको आज्ञा नमान्नु नै पाप हो। पापले मानिस र परमेश्वरको सङ्गति भाँच्यो।','Parameshwarko aagyaa namaannu nai paap ho. Paaple maanis ra Parameshwarko sangati bhaanchyo.','Turning from God’s command — that is sin. And sin broke the fellowship between humanity and God.','Genesis 3:8–10'],
['परमेश्वरले भन्नुभएको कुरा दुःखसाथ पूरा भयो। उहाँले तिनीहरूलाई अदन छोड्न भन्नुभयो — र त्यही दिनदेखि मानिस र परमेश्वरको बीचमा अलगाव आयो। तैपनि उहाँले प्रतिज्ञा दिनुभयो — एक दिन एक जना उद्धारक आउनुहुनेछ।','Parameshwarle bhannubhaeko kuraa dukhasaath puraa bhayo. Uhaanle tiniharulaai Adan chhodna bhannubhayo — ra tyahi dindekhi maanis ra Parameshwarko beechmaa alagaaw aayo. Taipani uhaanle pratigyaa dinubhayo — ek din ek janaa uddhaarak aaunuhunechha.','What God had said would happen, sadly happened. He told them to leave Eden — and from that day there has been a separation between humanity and God. Yet he gave a promise: one day a Rescuer would come.','Genesis 3:15']]},
{id:'spread',t:'Sin spreads',ne:'पाप फैलियो',art:FNE_ART.spread,
note:['पाप कहिल्यै एक्लै बस्दैन — त्यो परिवार र समाजभरि फैलिन्छ। तर परमेश्वरले बढ्दो खराबीलाई अनुग्रहले जवाफ दिनुहुन्छ — जहाज र इन्द्रेणीको प्रतिज्ञा।','Paap kahilyai eklai basdaina — tyo pariwaar ra samaajbhari phailinchha. Tara Parameshwarle badhdo kharaabilaai anugrahale jawaaph dinuhunchha — jahaaj ra indreniko pratigyaa.','Sin never stays private — it spreads through families and whole societies. Yet God answers growing evil with grace: the ark, and the rainbow promise.'],
paras:[
['पाप संसारभरि फैलियो। मानिसको मन परमेश्वरबाट टाढा भयो।','Paap sansaarbhari phailiyo. Maanisko man Parameshwarbaata taadhaa bhayo.','Sin spread through the whole world, and the human heart drifted far from God.','Genesis 4–6'],
['बगैंचा बाहिरको पहिलो परिवारमै त्यो देखियो — दाजु कयिनले डाहले भरिएर आफ्नै भाइ हाबिललाई मार्यो। कथाको पहिलो मृत्यु नै हत्या थियो।','Bagainchaa baahirako pahilo pariwaarmai tyo dekhiyo — daaju Kayinle daahale bhariera aaphnai bhaai Haabillaai maaryo. Kathaako pahilo mrityu nai hatyaa thiyo.','It showed in the very first family outside the garden: the elder brother, Cain, filled with envy, killed his own brother Abel. The first death in the story was a murder.','Genesis 4:8'],
['मानिसको खराबी देखेर परमेश्वरको हृदय दुख्यो। हाम्रो पापले उहाँलाई साँच्चै चोट पुर्याउँछ।','Maanisko kharaabi dekhera Parameshwarko hridaya dukhyo. Haamro paaple uhaanlaai saanchchai chot puryaunchha.','When God saw the evil of humanity, his heart was grieved. Our sin truly wounds him.','Genesis 6:5–6'],
['संसार हिंसाले यति भरियो कि परमेश्वरले त्यसलाई ठूलो बाढीले धुने निर्णय गर्नुभयो। तर एक जना विश्वासयोग्य मानिस थिए — नोआ। परमेश्वरले तिनलाई एउटा विशाल जहाज बनाउन लगाउनुभयो।','Sansaar hinsaale yati bhariyo ki Parameshwarle tyaslaai thulo baadhile dhune nirnaya garnubhayo. Tara ek janaa vishwaasyogya maanis thie — Noaa. Parameshwarle tinlaai eutaa vishaal jahaaj banaauna lagaunubhayo.','The world filled with such violence that God resolved to wash it clean with a great flood. But there was one faithful man — Noah. God had him build an enormous boat.','Genesis 6:11–14'],
['तैपनि परमेश्वरले संसारलाई छोड्नुभएन। नोआको परिवारमाथि उहाँले अनुग्रह देखाउनुभयो।','Taipani Parameshwarle sansaarlaai chhodnubhaena. Noaako pariwaarmaathi uhaanle anugraha dekhaunubhayo.','Even so, God did not abandon the world. He showed grace to Noah and his family.','Genesis 6–9'],
['बाढीपछि परमेश्वरले आकाशमा इन्द्रेणी राख्नुभयो — नाश होइन, प्रतिज्ञाको चिन्ह।','Baadhipachhi Parameshwarle aakaashmaa indreni raakhnubhayo — naash hoina, pratigyaako chinha.','After the flood God set a rainbow in the sky — a sign not of destruction, but of promise.','Genesis 9:12–16'],
['नोआबाट परमेश्वरले संसारलाई नयाँ सुरुवात दिनुभयो — ठीकसँग जिउने एउटा नयाँ मानिस-परिवार। तर मानिसको हृदय भने उस्तै रह्यो। पाप फेरि फैलिन थाल्यो — नयाँ सुरुवातले मात्र पुगेन।','Noaabaata Parameshwarle sansaarlaai nayaan suruwaat dinubhayo — theeksanga jiune eutaa nayaan maanis-pariwaar. Tara maanisko hridaya bhane ustai rahyo. Paap pheri phailina thaalyo — nayaan suruwaatle maatra pugena.','Through Noah God gave the world a fresh start — a new human family meant to live rightly. But the human heart stayed the same. Sin began to spread again — a fresh start alone was not enough.','Genesis 9:20–21 · 11'],
['धेरै पछि मानिसहरू एउटा ठाउँमा भेला भए र आकाशसम्म पुग्ने धरहरा बनाउन थाले — परमेश्वरविना नै ठूलो बन्न। त्यो ठाउँको नाम बाबेल थियो।','Dherai pachhi maanisharu eutaa thaaunmaa bhelaa bhae ra aakaashsamma pugne dharaharaa banaauna thaale — Parameshwarwinaa nai thulo banna. Tyo thaaunko naam Baabel thiyo.','Much later, people gathered in one place and began building a tower to reach the sky — to become great without God. The place was called Babel.','Genesis 11:1–4'],
['बाबेलमा मानिसहरूले आफ्नै नाम ठूलो बनाउन खोजे। तर परमेश्वरको योजना अझै अगाडि बढिरहेको थियो।','Baabelmaa maanisharule aaphnai naam thulo banaauna khoje. Tara Parameshwarko yojanaa ajhai agaadi badhiraheko thiyo.','At Babel people tried to make their own name great. But God’s plan kept moving forward.','Genesis 11'],
['परमेश्वरले भाषाहरू छुट्याउनुभयो र मानिसहरू संसारभरि छरिए। अब कथालाई एउटा नयाँ सुरुवात चाहिन्थ्यो।','Parameshwarle bhaashaaharu chhutyaunubhayo ra maanisharu sansaarbhari chharie. Aba kathaalaai eutaa nayaan suruwaat chaahinthyo.','God divided the languages and the peoples scattered across the earth. The story needed a new beginning.','Genesis 11:8–9']]},
{id:'abraham',t:'A promise to Abraham',ne:'अब्राहामलाई प्रतिज्ञा',art:FNE_ART.abraham,
note:['भाँचिएको संसारको लागि परमेश्वरको जवाफ — एउटा साधारण परिवार। अब्राहामद्वारा सबै जातिले आशिष् पाउने प्रतिज्ञा नै सुसमाचारको बीउ हो — र त्यो नेपालसम्म पनि आइपुग्छ।','Bhaanchieko sansaarko laagi Parameshwarko jawaaph — eutaa saadhaaran pariwaar. Abrahaamdwaaraa sabai jaatile aashish paaune pratigyaa nai susamaachaarko biu ho — ra tyo Nepaalsamma pani aaipugchha.','God’s answer to a broken world is, surprisingly, one ordinary family. The promise that ALL nations would be blessed through Abraham is the seed of the whole gospel — and it reaches Nepal too.'],
paras:[
['ती छरिएका जातिहरूका बीचबाट — नोआकै सन्तानमध्येबाट — परमेश्वरले एक जना मानिसलाई छान्नुभयो — अब्राहाम, ऊर भन्ने शहरका एक साधारण मानिस।','Ti chhariekaa jaatiharukaa beechbaata — Noaakai santaanmadhyebaata — Parameshwarle ek janaa maanislaai chhaannubhayo — Abrahaam, Ur bhanne shaharkaa ek saadhaaran maanis.','From among those scattered peoples — from the line of Noah himself — God chose one man: Abraham, an ordinary man from a city called Ur.','Genesis 11:31 · 12:1'],
['परमेश्वरले अब्राहामलाई बोलाउनुभयो — तिम्रो परिवारद्वारा संसारका सबै जातिले आशिष् पाउनेछन्।','Parameshwarle Abrahaamlaai bolaunubhayo — timro pariwaardwaaraa sansaarkaa sabai jaatile aashish paaunechhan.','God called Abraham: through your family, all the peoples of the earth will be blessed.','Genesis 12:1–3'],
['परमेश्वरले अब्राहामलाई किन छान्नुभयो? उनी अरूभन्दा धर्मी भएकाले होइन। परमेश्वर कृपामा धनी हुनुहुन्छ र मानिसजातिलाई बचाउन चाहनुहुन्थ्यो। हामीले उहाँलाई छोड्ने हरेक कारण दिएका थियौं — तैपनि आफ्नो महान् प्रेम र उदारताको कारण उहाँले हामीलाई छोड्नुभएन।','Parameshwarle Abrahaamlaai kina chhaannubhayo? Uni arubhandaa dharmi bhaekaale hoina. Parameshwar kripaamaa dhani hunuhunchha ra maanisjaatilaai bachaauna chaahanuhunthyo. Haamile uhaanlaai chhodne harek kaaran diekaa thiyaun — taipani aaphno mahaan prem ra udaarataako kaaran uhaanle haamilaai chhodnubhaena.','Why did God choose Abraham? Not because he was more righteous than others. God is rich in mercy, and he wanted to save humanity. We had given him every reason to abandon us — yet because of his great love and generosity, he did not.','Ephesians 2:4 · Deuteronomy 7:7–8'],
['अब्राहामले आफ्नो घर, आफ्नो देश छोडेर हिँडे — कहाँ जाने भन्ने पनि थाहा थिएन। विश्वास भनेको यस्तै हिँडाइ हो।','Abrahaamle aaphno ghar, aaphno desh chhodera hinde — kahaan jaane bhanne pani thaahaa thiena. Vishwaas bhaneko yastai hindaai ho.','Abraham left his home and his country without even knowing where he was going. That walk is what faith looks like.','Hebrews 11:8'],
['एक रात परमेश्वरले उनलाई बाहिर लैजानुभयो — आकाशका ताराहरू गन। तिम्रा सन्तान त्यति नै हुनेछन्।','Ek raat Parameshwarle unlaai baahira laijaanubhayo — aakaashkaa taaraaharu gana. Timraa santaan tyati nai hunechhan.','One night God led him outside: count the stars, if you can. So many will your children be.','Genesis 15:5'],
['अब्राहामले परमेश्वरलाई विश्वास गरे, र परमेश्वरले उनलाई धर्मी ठहराउनुभयो।','Abrahaamle Parameshwarlaai vishwaas gare, ra Parameshwarle unlaai dharmi thaharaunubhayo.','Abraham trusted God — and God counted him as righteous.','Genesis 15:6'],
['तर एउटा समस्या थियो — अब्राहाम र उनकी पत्नी सारा वृद्ध थिए, र तिनीहरूको कुनै सन्तान थिएन। प्रतिज्ञा असम्भवजस्तो सुनिन्थ्यो। तैपनि ठीक समयमा साराले छोरो जन्माइन् — इसहाक, जसको नामको अर्थ हो हाँसो। परमेश्वरको लागि असम्भव केही रहेनछ।','Tara eutaa samasyaa thiyo — Abrahaam ra unki patni Saaraa vriddha thie, ra tiniharuko kunai santaan thiena. Pratigyaa asambhawjasto suninthyo. Taipani theek samayamaa Saaraale chhoro janmaain — Isahaak, jasko naamko artha ho haanso. Parameshwarko laagi asambhaw kehi rahenachha.','But there was a problem: Abraham and his wife Sarah were old, and they had no child at all. The promise sounded impossible. Yet at just the right time Sarah bore a son — Isaac, whose name means laughter. Nothing, it turned out, is impossible for God.','Genesis 18:10–14 · 21:1–6'],
['यही एउटा परिवारबाट परमेश्वरको उद्धारको कथा अगाडि बढ्यो।','Yahi eutaa pariwaarbaata Parameshwarko uddhaarko kathaa agaadi badhyo.','From this one family, God’s rescue story moved forward.','Genesis 12–50'],
['त्यस जमानामा मानिसहरू परमेश्वरलाई भेटी चढाउँथे — यसलाई बलि भनिन्छ। एक दिन परमेश्वरले अब्राहामको विश्वासको ठूलो जाँच गर्नुभयो — तर ठीक समयमा, डाँडामाथि, उहाँले आफैँ बलिको थुमा जुटाइदिनुभयो। त्यो दिनदेखि यो भनाइ चल्यो — परमेश्वरले जुटाउनुहुनेछ।','Tyas jamaanaamaa maanisharu Parameshwarlaai bheti chadhaunthe — yaslaai bali bhaninchha. Ek din Parameshwarle Abrahaamko vishwaasko thulo jaanch garnubhayo — tara theek samayamaa, daandaamaathi, uhaanle aaphain baliko thumaa jutaaidinubhayo. Tyo dindekhi yo bhanaai chalyo — Parameshwarle jutaunuhunechha.','In those days people brought offerings to God — gifts called sacrifices. One day God tested Abraham’s faith deeply — and at just the right moment, on the mountain, God himself provided the lamb for the sacrifice. From that day a saying spread: the LORD will provide.','Genesis 22:8–14']]},
{id:'exodus',t:'Rescue from Egypt',ne:'मिश्रबाट छुटकारा',art:FNE_ART.exodus,
note:['निस्तारले सारा बाइबलको ढाँचा देखाउँछ — उद्धार सट्टामा आउने बलिबाट आउँछ। इस्राएल बलियो भएर होइन, थुमा मरेकोले र परमेश्वरले प्रतिज्ञा पूरा गर्नुभएकोले स्वतन्त्र भयो।','Nistaarle saaraa Baibalko dhaanchaa dekhaunchha — uddhaar sattaamaa aaune balibaata aaunchha. Israel baliyo bhaera hoina, thumaa marekole ra Parameshwarle pratigyaa puraa garnubhaekole swatantra bhayo.','The Passover paints the pattern of the whole Bible: rescue comes through a substitute. Israel walked free not because they were strong, but because a lamb died in their place and God kept his promise.'],
paras:[
['समय बित्दै जाँदा अब्राहामको परिवार बढेर ठूलो जाति बन्यो — त्यस जातिको नाम इस्राएल हो। तर तिनीहरू मिश्र भन्ने देशमा पुगे, र त्यहाँका राजाले तिनीहरूलाई कमारा बनाए। चार सय वर्षसम्म तिनीहरूले दुःख पाए। तिनीहरूले परमेश्वरलाई पुकारे — र उहाँले सुन्नुभयो।','Samaya bitdai jaandaa Abrahaamko pariwaar badhera thulo jaati banyo — tyas jaatiko naam Israel ho. Tara tiniharu Mishra bhanne deshmaa puge, ra tyahaankaa raajaale tiniharulaai kamaaraa banaae. Chaar saya barshasamma tiniharule dukha paae. Tiniharule Parameshwarlaai pukaare — ra uhaanle sunnubhayo.','As time passed, Abraham’s family grew into a great people — a people called Israel. But they ended up in a country called Egypt, and its king made them slaves. For four hundred years they suffered. They cried out to God — and he heard.','Exodus 1 · 2:23–25'],
['परमेश्वरले जलिरहेको पोथ्राबाट मोशालाई बोलाउनुभयो — मैले आफ्ना मानिसहरूको दुःख देखेको छु। जाऊ, तिनीहरूलाई निकालेर ल्याऊ।','Parameshwarle jaliraheko pothraabaata Moshaalaai bolaunubhayo — maile aaphnaa maanisharuko dukha dekheko chhu. Jaau, tiniharulaai nikaalera lyaau.','From a burning bush God called Moses: I have seen the suffering of my people. Go, and bring them out.','Exodus 3'],
['मिश्रको राजाले तिनीहरूलाई जान दिएन। अन्तिम रातमा मृत्यु मिश्रभरि आयो — तर परमेश्वरले भन्नुभयो — थुमाको रगतले ढोकामा चिन्ह लगाओ, र मृत्यु तिमीहरूको घर नाघेर जानेछ। यसैलाई निस्तार भनिन्छ।','Mishrako raajaale tiniharulaai jaana diena. Antim raatmaa mrityu Mishrabhari aayo — tara Parameshwarle bhannubhayo — thumaako ragatle dhokaamaa chinha lagaao, ra mrityu timiharuko ghar naaghera jaanechha. Yasailaai nistaar bhaninchha.','The king of Egypt refused to let them go. On the final night death came through Egypt — but God said: mark your doors with the blood of a lamb, and death will pass over your house. That night is called the Passover.','Exodus 11–12'],
['थुमाको रगतले तिनीहरूलाई मृत्युबाट बचायो। परमेश्वरले आफ्ना मानिसहरूलाई छुटाउनुभयो।','Thumaako ragatle tiniharulaai mrityubaata bachaayo. Parameshwarle aaphnaa maanisharulaai chhutaunubhayo.','The blood of a lamb sheltered them from death, and God set his people free.','Exodus 12'],
['समुद्रको अगाडि बाटो थिएन — तर परमेश्वरले पानी नै दुई भाग पार्नुभयो, र मानिसहरू सुक्खा जमिनमा हिँडेर पार गए।','Samudrako agaadi baato thiena — tara Parameshwarle paani nai dui bhaag paarnubhayo, ra maanisharu sukkhaa jaminmaa hindera paar gae.','At the sea there was no way through — but God parted the very waters, and the people walked across on dry ground.','Exodus 14'],
['परमेश्वरले तिनीहरूसँग करार बाँध्नुभयो र तिनीहरूकै बीचमा बास गर्नुभयो।','Parameshwarle tiniharusanga karaar baandhnubhayo ra tiniharukai beechmaa baas garnubhayo.','God made a covenant with them and came to dwell right among his people.','Exodus 19–40'],
['करार भनेको साधारण वाचा होइन — विवाहजस्तै दुई पक्षलाई जोड्ने गहिरो प्रतिज्ञा हो। परमेश्वरले भन्नुभयो — म तिमीहरूको परमेश्वर हुनेछु, र तिमीहरू मेरा मानिसहरू हुनेछौ।','Karaar bhaneko saadhaaran waachaa hoina — vivaahajastai dui pakshalaai jodne gahiro pratigyaa ho. Parameshwarle bhannubhayo — ma timiharuko Parameshwar hunechhu, ra timiharu meraa maanisharu hunechhau.','A covenant is no casual promise — it is a deep, binding pledge that joins two parties, like a marriage. God said: I will be your God, and you will be my people.','Exodus 6:7 · 19:5'],
['उजाडस्थानमा परमेश्वरले तिनीहरूलाई छोड्नुभएन — आकाशबाट रोटी, चट्टानबाट पानी, र बाटो देखाउने आगोको खामो।','Ujaadsthaanmaa Parameshwarle tiniharulaai chhodnubhaena — aakaashbaata roti, chattaanbaata paani, ra baato dekhaaune aagoko khaamo.','In the wilderness God did not leave them: bread from heaven, water from the rock, and a pillar of fire to show the way.','Exodus 16–17 · 13:21'],
['मोशापछि यहोशू नाम गरेका अगुवाले इस्राएललाई प्रतिज्ञाको देशमा डोर्याए। यर्दन नदी तरेर तिनीहरू भित्र पसे — र परमेश्वर आफैँ तिनीहरूका लागि लड्नुभयो। अग्ला पर्खालले घेरिएको यरीहो शहर पनि तरवारले होइन, उहाँकै शक्तिले ढल्यो।','Moshaapachhi Yahoshu naam garekaa aguwaale Israellaai pratigyaako deshmaa doryaae. Yardan nadi tarera tiniharu bhitra pase — ra Parameshwar aaphain tiniharukaa laagi ladnubhayo. Aglaa parkhaalle gherieko Yariho shahar pani tarwaarle hoina, uhaankai shaktile dhalyo.','After Moses, a leader named Joshua led Israel into the promised land. They crossed the Jordan river and went in — and God himself fought for them. Even Jericho, a city ringed by high walls, fell not by the sword but by his power.','Joshua 1 · 3 · 6']]},
{id:'kings',t:'Kings and prophets',ne:'राजा र अगमवक्ताहरू',art:FNE_ART.kings,
note:['हरेक राजा असफल हुन्छ — र त्यही नै मुख्य कुरा हो। कथाले हामीलाई अझ असल राजाको प्रतीक्षा गर्न सिकाउँछ — जसको राज्य कहिल्यै सिद्धिँदैन।','Harek raajaa asaphal hunchha — ra tyahi nai mukhya kuraa ho. Kathaale haamilaai ajha asal raajaako pratikshaa garna sikaunchha — jasko raajya kahilyai siddhindaina.','Every king fails — and that is the point. The story is training us to long for a better King, whose kingdom never ends.'],
paras:[
['मिश्रबाट निस्केपछि परमेश्वरले इस्राएललाई प्रतिज्ञा गरिएको देशमा ल्याउनुभयो। त्यहाँ तिनीहरू बसे, र समय बित्दै जाँदा तिनीहरूले भने — अरू जातिहरूका जस्तै हामीलाई पनि राजा चाहिन्छ।','Mishrabaata niskepachhi Parameshwarle Israellaai pratigyaa garieko deshmaa lyaunubhayo. Tyahaan tiniharu base, ra samaya bitdai jaandaa tiniharule bhane — aru jaatiharukaa jastai haamilaai pani raajaa chaahinchha.','After Egypt, God brought Israel into the land he had promised. There they settled — and in time they said: give us a king, like all the other nations have.','Joshua · 1 Samuel 8'],
['इस्राएलका राजाहरूमध्ये सबैभन्दा प्रिय दाऊद थिए। राजा हुनुअघि उनी त एउटा सानो गोठालो केटो मात्र थिए — तर परमेश्वरले उनलाई छान्नुभयो। मानिस बाहिरी रूप हेर्छ; परमेश्वर हृदय हेर्नुहुन्छ।','Israelkaa raajaaharumadhye sabaibhandaa priya Daaud thie. Raajaa hunuaghi uni ta eutaa saano gothaalo keto maatra thie — tara Parameshwarle unlaai chhaannubhayo. Maanis baahiri roop herchha; Parameshwar hridaya hernuhunchha.','The best-loved of Israel’s kings was a man named David. Before he was king he was only a young shepherd boy — but God chose him. People look at the outside; God looks at the heart.','1 Samuel 16:7'],
['केटै छँदा दाऊदले गोल्यत नाम गरेको विशाल शत्रु-योद्धालाई एउटै ढुङ्गाले पराजित गरे — तरवारले होइन, परमेश्वरको नाममा। सारा इस्राएलले देख्यो — साँचो बल परमेश्वरबाट आउँछ।','Ketai chhandaa Daaudle Golyat naam gareko vishaal shatru-yoddhaalaai eutai dhungaale paraajit gare — tarwaarle hoina, Parameshwarko naammaa. Saaraa Israelle dekhyo — saancho bal Parameshwarbaata aaunchha.','While still a boy, David felled a giant enemy warrior named Goliath with a single stone — not by the sword, but in the name of God. All Israel saw it: true strength comes from God.','1 Samuel 17:45–50'],
['परमेश्वरले दाऊदलाई राजा बनाउनुभयो र प्रतिज्ञा दिनुभयो — तिम्रो वंशबाट एउटा अनन्त राजा आउनुहुनेछ।','Parameshwarle Daaudlaai raajaa banaunubhayo ra pratigyaa dinubhayo — timro wanshabaata eutaa ananta raajaa aaunuhunechha.','God made David king and promised: from your line will come a King whose kingdom never ends.','2 Samuel 7'],
['दाऊदपछि सयौं वर्षसम्म इस्राएलमा धेरै राजाहरूले राज्य गरे। कोही असल थिए — तर धेरैजसो गहिरो पापमा जिए। तिनीहरूले झूटा देवताहरू पुजे, गरिबहरूलाई थिचे, र मानिसहरूलाई पनि परमेश्वरबाट टाढा डोर्याए।','Daaudpachhi sayaun barshasamma Israelmaa dherai raajaaharule raajya gare. Kohi asal thie — tara dheraijaso gahiro paapmaa jie. Tiniharule jhutaa dewataaharu puje, garibharulaai thiche, ra maanisharulaai pani Parameshwarbaata taadhaa doryaae.','After David, many kings ruled Israel over hundreds of years. A few were good — but most lived in deep sin. They worshiped false gods, crushed the poor, and led the people far from God.','1–2 Kings'],
['यो एउटा दुःखलाग्दो चक्र थियो। मानिसहरू केही समय परमेश्वरसँग हिँड्थे; अनि बिस्तारै सम्झौता गर्दै झूटा देवताहरूतिर फर्कन्थे; त्यसले तिनीहरूलाई शत्रुको थिचोमिचोमा पुर्याउँथ्यो; दुःखमा तिनीहरू परमेश्वरलाई पुकार्थे — र उहाँले बचाउनुहुन्थ्यो। तर केही समयपछि फेरि त्यही चक्र दोहोरिन्थ्यो।','Yo eutaa dukhalaagdo chakra thiyo. Maanisharu kehi samaya Parameshwarsanga hindthe; ani bistaarai samjhautaa gardai jhutaa dewataaharutira pharkanthe; tyasle tiniharulaai shatruko thichomichomaa puryaunthyo; dukhamaa tiniharu Parameshwarlaai pukaarthe — ra uhaanle bachaunuhunthyo. Tara kehi samayapachhi pheri tyahi chakra dohorinthyo.','It was a heartbreaking cycle. For a while the people would walk with God; then slowly they would compromise and turn to false gods; that led them into oppression under their enemies; in their misery they would cry out to God — and he would save them. And then, after a while, the same circle would begin again.','Judges 2:11–19'],
['ती राजाहरूकै समयमा परमेश्वरले अगमवक्ताहरू पठाउनुहुन्थ्यो — उहाँले छान्नुभएका मानिसहरू, जसले राजा र जनतासामु परमेश्वरको वचन बोल्थे। तिनीहरूले चेतावनी दिन्थे — पाप छोड, परमेश्वरतिर फर्क — र आशाको सन्देश पनि सुनाउँथे।','Ti raajaaharukai samayamaa Parameshwarle agamwaktaaharu pathaunuhunthyo — uhaanle chhaannubhaekaa maanisharu, jasle raajaa ra janataasaamu Parameshwarko wachan bolthe. Tiniharule chetaawani dinthe — paap chhoda, Parameshwartira pharka — ra aashaako sandesh pani sunaunthe.','And all through the years of those kings, God kept sending prophets — people God chose to speak his words to the kings and to the people. They brought warning — turn from sin, come back to God — and they brought hope.','2 Kings 17:13'],
['अगमवक्ताहरूले भने — परमेश्वरले नयाँ करार बाँध्नुहुनेछ, र उहाँको सेवकले हाम्रो पाप बोक्नुहुनेछ।','Agamwaktaaharule bhane — Parameshwarle nayaan karaar baandhnuhunechha, ra uhaanko sewakle haamro paap boknuhunechha.','The prophets spoke of hope: God will make a new covenant, and his Servant will carry our sin.','Jeremiah 31 · Isaiah 53'],
['परमेश्वरले अगमवक्ताद्वारा भन्नुभयो — म तिमीहरूलाई नयाँ हृदय दिनेछु, र आफ्नो आत्मा तिमीहरूभित्र राख्नेछु।','Parameshwarle agamwaktaadwaaraa bhannubhayo — ma timiharulaai nayaan hridaya dinechhu, ra aaphno aatmaa timiharubhitra raakhnechhu.','Through the prophets God promised: I will give you a new heart, and I will put my own Spirit within you.','Ezekiel 36:26–27'],
['तर धेरैजसो राजा र जनताले सुनेनन्। अन्त्यमा त्यही पापको फल आयो — शत्रुको सेनाले देश जित्यो, र इस्राएलका मानिसहरूले आफ्नै देश छोड्नुपर्यो। यही नै त्यो अनुशासन थियो, जसको बारेमा अगमवक्ताहरूले वर्षौंदेखि चेतावनी दिएका थिए।','Tara dheraijaso raajaa ra janataale sunenan. Antyamaa tyahi paapko phal aayo — shatruko senaale desh jityo, ra Israelkaa maanisharule aaphnai desh chhodnuparyo. Yahi nai tyo anushaasan thiyo, jasko baaremaa agamwaktaaharule barshaundekhi chetaawani diekaa thie.','But most of the kings and the people would not listen. In the end sin bore its fruit: an enemy army conquered the land, and the people of Israel were forced to leave their own country. This was the discipline the prophets had warned about for years.','2 Kings 17 · 25']]},
{id:'wait',t:'The long wait',ne:'लामो प्रतीक्षा',art:FNE_ART.wait,
note:['परमेश्वरको मौनता उहाँको अनुपस्थिति होइन। चुपचाप बितेका चार सय वर्ष इतिहासकै सबैभन्दा ठूलो आगमनको तयारीले भरिएका थिए।','Parameshwarko maunataa uhaanko anupasthiti hoina. Chupchaap bitekaa chaar saya barsha itihaaskai sabaibhandaa thulo aagamanko tayaarile bhariekaa thie.','God’s silences are not absences. Four hundred quiet years were full of preparation for the greatest arrival in history.'],
paras:[
['यसरी अगमवक्ताहरूको चेतावनी पूरा भयो — इस्राएलका मानिसहरू आफ्नो देशबाट टाढा लगिए। घर, खेतबारी, छिमेक — सबै पछाडि छुट्यो। सबै आशा हराएजस्तो देखियो।','Yasari agamwaktaaharuko chetaawani puraa bhayo — Israelkaa maanisharu aaphno deshbaata taadhaa lagie. Ghar, khetbaari, chhimek — sabai pachhaadi chhutyo. Sabai aashaa haraaejasto dekhiyo.','So the prophets’ warning came true: the people of Israel were carried far from their own land. Home, fields, neighbors — everything was left behind. It looked as if all hope was lost.','2 Kings 25'],
['यसैलाई निर्वासन भनिन्छ — बेबिलोन देशको सेनाले यरूशलेम भत्कायो, परमेश्वरको मन्दिर जलायो, र मानिसहरूलाई कैद गरेर आफ्नो देशमा लगे।','Yasailaai nirwaasan bhaninchha — Bebilon deshko senaale Yarushalem bhatkaayo, Parameshwarko mandir jalaayo, ra maanisharulaai kaid garera aaphno deshmaa lage.','This is called the exile: the armies of Babylon tore down Jerusalem, burned God’s temple, and carried the people away captive to their own land.','2 Kings 25:8–11'],
['निर्वासनमा पनि परमेश्वरले भन्नुभयो — मसँग तिमीहरूको निम्ति शान्तिका योजनाहरू छन्, आशा दिने योजनाहरू।','Nirwaasanmaa pani Parameshwarle bhannubhayo — masanga timiharuko nimti shaantikaa yojanaaharu chhan, aashaa dine yojanaaharu.','Even in exile God said: I know the plans I have for you — plans of peace, plans full of hope.','Jeremiah 29:11'],
['इतिहासले एउटा कुरा प्रस्टै देखाइसकेको थियो — हामी मानिसहरू आफ्नै बलले परमेश्वरसँग विश्वासयोग्य भएर हिँड्न सक्दा रहेनछौं; हाम्रो विद्रोह दोहोरिइरह्यो। हामीलाई अर्कै उत्तर चाहिन्थ्यो। परमेश्वरले अगमवक्ताद्वारा त्यही उत्तरको प्रतिज्ञा गर्नुभयो — म तिमीहरूको ढुङ्गाको हृदय निकालेर मासुको हृदय दिनेछु, र मेरो व्यवस्था तिमीहरूकै हृदयमा लेखिदिनेछु।','Itihaasle eutaa kuraa prastai dekhaaisakeko thiyo — haami maanisharu aaphnai balle Parameshwarsanga vishwaasyogya bhaera hindna sakdaa rahenachhaun; haamro vidroha dohoriirahyo. Haamilaai arkai uttar chaahinthyo. Parameshwarle agamwaktaadwaaraa tyahi uttarko pratigyaa garnubhayo — ma timiharuko dhungaako hridaya nikaalera maasuko hridaya dinechhu, ra mero vyawasthaa timiharukai hridayamaa lekhidinechhu.','History had made one thing plain: we humans could not stay faithful to God in our own strength — our rebellion kept repeating. We needed a different answer. And through the prophets God promised exactly that: I will take out your heart of stone and give you a heart of flesh, and I will write my law on your very hearts.','Ezekiel 36:26 · Jeremiah 31:33'],
['अगमवक्ता इजकिएलले एउटा दर्शन देखे — सुकेका हड्डीहरूले भरिएको एउटा बेँसी। परमेश्वरले सोध्नुभयो — के यी हड्डीहरू फेरि जीवित हुन सक्छन्? अनि उहाँको सासले ती हड्डीहरूमा जीवन भरिदियो, र त्यहाँ एउटा ठूलो जमात उभियो। चिन्ह प्रस्ट थियो — मरेतुल्य हृदयलाई पनि परमेश्वरले फेरि जीवित पार्न सक्नुहुन्छ।','Agamwaktaa Ijakielle eutaa darshan dekhe — sukekaa haddiharule bharieko eutaa bensi. Parameshwarle sodhnubhayo — ke yi haddiharu pheri jeewit huna sakchhan? Ani uhaanko saasle ti haddiharumaa jeewan bharidiyo, ra tyahaan eutaa thulo jamaat ubhiyo. Chinha prasta thiyo — maretulya hridayalaai pani Parameshwarle pheri jeewit paarna saknuhunchha.','The prophet Ezekiel saw a vision: a valley full of dry bones. God asked him — can these bones live again? Then God’s own breath filled those bones with life, and a great multitude stood up. The sign was clear: even a heart as good as dead, God can bring back to life.','Ezekiel 37:1–10'],
['निर्वासनमा लगिएकाहरूमध्ये दानिएल नाम गरेका एक जना युवा थिए। त्यो विदेशी देशमा, प्रार्थना गर्न निषेध हुँदा पनि, उनले दिनको तीन पटक झ्याल खोलेर प्रार्थना गरिरहे। सिंहहरूको खोरमा फालिँदा पनि परमेश्वरले उनलाई बचाउनुभयो।','Nirwaasanmaa lagiekaaharumadhye Daaniel naam garekaa ek janaa yuwaa thie. Tyo videshi deshmaa, praarthanaa garna nishedh hundaa pani, unle dinko teen patak jhyaal kholera praarthanaa garirahe. Sinhaharuko khormaa phaalindaa pani Parameshwarle unlaai bachaunubhayo.','Among those carried into exile was a young man named Daniel. In that foreign land, even when prayer was outlawed, he kept opening his window to pray three times a day. Even when he was thrown into a den of lions, God kept him safe.','Daniel 6'],
['सत्तरी वर्षपछि, प्रतिज्ञा अनुसार, परमेश्वरले तिनीहरूलाई आफ्नै देशमा फर्काउनुभयो। तिनीहरूले यरूशलेम शहर र मन्दिर फेरि बनाए। तर हृदयको गहिराइमा सबैले बुझेका थिए — सबैभन्दा ठूलो प्रतिज्ञा अझै पूरा भएको छैन।','Sattari barshapachhi, pratigyaa anusaar, Parameshwarle tiniharulaai aaphnai deshmaa pharkaunubhayo. Tiniharule Yarushalem shahar ra mandir pheri banaae. Tara hridayako gahiraaimaa sabaile bujhekaa thie — sabaibhandaa thulo pratigyaa ajhai puraa bhaeko chhaina.','Seventy years later, just as promised, God brought them back to their own land. They rebuilt the city of Jerusalem and the temple. But deep down everyone knew: the greatest promise had not yet been kept.','Ezra · Nehemiah'],
['तैपनि तिनीहरूले पर्खिरहे — प्रतिज्ञा गरिएको उद्धारक, मसीह, कहिले आउनुहुन्छ?','Taipani tiniharule parkhirahe — pratigyaa garieko uddhaarak, Maseeh, kahile aaunuhunchha?','Still they waited: when would the promised Rescuer — the Messiah — come?','Isaiah 9:6–7'],
['तर त्यो कसरी हुनेछ भन्ने कसैलाई थाहा थिएन। धेरै इस्राएलीहरूले एक जना लडाकु वीरको प्रतीक्षा गरे, जसले तिनीहरूलाई थिचोमिचो गर्नेहरूबाट छुटाउनेछ। तर साँचो उत्तर त्योभन्दा धेरै गहिरो थियो — पापबाटै छुटाउनुहुने उद्धारक। परमेश्वर आफैँ आफ्नो मन्दिरमा फर्कनुहुनेथियो — र मानिसको जीवन र स्वतन्त्रताको लागि आफ्नै ज्यान अर्पण गर्नुहुनेथियो।','Tara tyo kasari hunechha bhanne kasailaai thaahaa thiena. Dherai Israeliharule ek janaa ladaaku veerko pratikshaa gare, jasle tiniharulaai thichomicho garneharubaata chhutaaunechha. Tara saancho uttar tyobhandaa dherai gahiro thiyo — paapbaatai chhutaaunuhune uddhaarak. Parameshwar aaphain aaphno mandirmaa pharkanuhunethiyo — ra maanisko jeewan ra swatantrataako laagi aaphnai jyaan arpan garnuhunethiyo.','But nobody knew how it would happen. Many in Israel waited for a warrior who would deliver them from their oppressors. The true answer ran far deeper — a deliverer who would free them from their sins. God himself would return to his temple — and lay down his own life for the life and freedom of human beings.','Malachi 3:1 · Mark 10:45'],
['चार सय वर्षसम्म सन्नाटा रह्यो। तर परमेश्वरले आफ्नो प्रतिज्ञा बिर्सनुभएको थिएन।','Chaar saya barshasamma sannaataa rahyo. Tara Parameshwarle aaphno pratigyaa birsanubhaeko thiena.','For four hundred years, silence. But God had not forgotten his promise.','Malachi → Matthew']]},
{id:'immanuel',t:'God with us',ne:'इम्मानुएल',art:FNE_ART.immanuel,
note:['सृष्टिकर्ता आफ्नै सृष्टिभित्र पस्नुभयो। येशूमा परमेश्वरले टाढाबाट सहायता पठाउनुभएन — उहाँ आफैँ आउनुभयो।','Srishtikartaa aaphnai srishtibhitra pasnubhayo. Yeshumaa Parameshwarle taadhaabaata sahaayataa pathaunubhaena — uhaan aaphain aaunubhayo.','The Creator stepped inside his own creation. In Jesus, God did not send help from a distance — he came himself.'],
paras:[
['अनि — त्यो लामो, चुपचाप प्रतीक्षापछि — येशू जन्मनुभयो। उहाँलाई अर्को नाम पनि दिइयो — इम्मानुएल, अर्थात् परमेश्वर हामीसँग।','Ani — tyo laamo, chupchaap pratikshaapachhi — Yeshu janmanubhayo. Uhaanlaai arko naam pani diiyo — Immaanuel, arthaat Parameshwar haamisanga.','And then — after that long, silent wait — Jesus was born. He was given another name too: Immanuel, which means God with us.','Matthew 1:23'],
['उहाँको जन्मअघि नै अगमवक्ताहरूले लेखेका थिए — हाम्रा निम्ति एउटा बालक जन्मनुहुनेछ, र उहाँलाई अचम्मको सल्लाहकार, शक्तिशाली परमेश्वर, अनन्तका पिता, शान्तिका राजकुमार भनिनेछ। उहाँ कन्याबाट जन्मनुहुनेछ भनेर पनि लेखिएको थियो — र ठीक त्यसै भयो।','Uhaanko janmaaghi nai agamwaktaaharule lekhekaa thie — haamraa nimti eutaa baalak janmanuhunechha, ra uhaanlaai achammako sallaahakaar, shaktishaali Parameshwar, anantakaa Pitaa, shaantikaa raajkumaar bhaninechha. Uhaan kanyaabaata janmanuhunechha bhanera pani lekhieko thiyo — ra theek tyasai bhayo.','Long before his birth the prophets had written: for us a child will be born, and he will be called Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace. It was also written that he would be born of a virgin — and that is exactly what happened.','Isaiah 9:6 · 7:14'],
['परमेश्वर आफैँ मानिस बन्नुभयो र हाम्रै बीचमा बस्नुभयो।','Parameshwar aaphain maanis bannubhayo ra haamrai beechmaa basnubhayo.','God himself became human and made his home among us.','John 1:14'],
['येशूले परमेश्वर को हुनुहुन्छ र कस्तो हुनुहुन्छ भनेर पूर्ण रूपमा प्रकट गर्नुभयो। उहाँलाई धेरै नामले चिनिन्छ — परमेश्वरको वचन, देह बन्नुभएको परमेश्वर, परमेश्वरका पुत्र। अनि उहाँ आफैँले भने आफूलाई प्रायः मानिसका पुत्र भन्नुहुन्थ्यो — दानिएल अगमवक्ताको दर्शनबाट आएको नाम, जहाँ सबै जाति र भाषाका मानिसहरूले उहाँको सेवा गर्छन्।','Yeshule Parameshwar ko hunuhunchha ra kasto hunuhunchha bhanera purna rupmaa prakat garnubhayo. Uhaanlaai dherai naamle chininchha — Parameshwarko wachan, deha bannubhaeko Parameshwar, Parameshwarkaa putra. Ani uhaan aaphaile bhane aaphulaai praayah maanisakaa putra bhannuhunthyo — Daaniel agamwaktaako darshanbaata aaeko naam, jahaan sabai jaati ra bhaashaakaa maanisharule uhaanko sewaa garchhan.','Jesus revealed perfectly who God is and what God is like. He is known by many names — the Word of God, God become flesh, the Son of God. And he himself most often used the name Son of Man — a name from the prophet Daniel’s vision, where people of every nation and language serve him.','John 1:1,14 · Daniel 7:13–14'],
['येशू दरबारमा होइन, नासरत भन्ने सानो गाउँमा हुर्कनुभयो। उहाँले काम गर्नुभयो, थकाइ जान्नुभयो, आँसु चिन्नुभयो — हाम्रो जीवन उहाँले भित्रैबाट बुझ्नुहुन्छ।','Yeshu darbaarmaa hoina, Naasarat bhanne saano gaaunmaa hurkanubhayo. Uhaanle kaam garnubhayo, thakaai jaannubhayo, aansu chinnubhayo — haamro jeewan uhaanle bhitraibaata bujhnuhunchha.','Jesus grew up not in a palace but in a small village called Nazareth. He worked, knew tiredness, knew tears — he understands our life from the inside.','Luke 2:39–52 · Hebrews 4:15'],
['येशूले परमेश्वरको राज्यको सुसमाचार सुनाउनुभयो र हराएकाहरूलाई खोज्नुभयो।','Yeshule Parameshwarko raajyako susamaachaar sunaunubhayo ra haraaekaaharulaai khojnubhayo.','Jesus announced the good news of God’s kingdom and went looking for the lost.','Luke 4 · Luke 19:10'],
['यूहन्ना नाम गरेका एक जना अगमवक्ता थिए, जसलाई परमेश्वरले मानिसहरूलाई तयार पार्न पठाउनुभएको थियो। येशूलाई देखेर तिनले कराएर भने — हेर, परमेश्वरको थुमा, जसले संसारको पाप उठाइलानुहुन्छ!','Yuhannaa naam garekaa ek janaa agamwaktaa thie, jaslaai Parameshwarle maanisharulaai tayaar paarna pathaunubhaeko thiyo. Yeshulaai dekhera tinle karaaera bhane — hera, Parameshwarko thumaa, jasle sansaarko paap uthaailaanuhunchha!','There was a prophet named John, sent by God to make the people ready. When John saw Jesus, he cried out: look — the Lamb of God, who takes away the sin of the world!','John 1:29']]},
{id:'crossgs',t:'The cross and the empty tomb',ne:'क्रूस र रित्तो चिहान',art:FNE_ART.cross,
note:['यहाँ अदनको भाँचिएको सङ्गतिको जवाफ छ। साँचो थुमाले हाम्रो पाप बोक्नुभयो, र रित्तो चिहान नै मोल पूरा तिरिएको प्रमाण हो।','Yahaan Adanko bhaanchieko sangatiko jawaaph chha. Saancho thumaale haamro paap boknubhayo, ra ritto chihaan nai mol puraa tirieko pramaan ho.','Here the broken fellowship of Eden is answered. The true Lamb carried our sin, and the empty tomb is the proof that the price was fully paid.'],
paras:[
['क्रूसको अघिल्लो रात येशूले बगैंचामा प्रार्थना गर्नुभयो — पिता, तपाईंकै इच्छा पूरा होस्। उहाँले आफ्नै खुशीले त्यो बाटो रोज्नुभयो।','Kroosko aghillo raat Yeshule bagainchaamaa praarthanaa garnubhayo — Pitaa, tapaainkai ichchhaa puraa hos. Uhaanle aaphnai khushile tyo baato rojnubhayo.','The night before the cross, Jesus prayed in a garden: Father, let your will be done. He chose that road willingly.','Luke 22:39–44'],
['भोलिपल्ट उहाँलाई पक्रेर मृत्युदण्ड दिइयो — क्रूसमा टाँगेर, त्यस समयको सबैभन्दा क्रूर सजाय। तर यो सबै परमेश्वरको योजनाभित्रै थियो।','Bholipalta uhaanlaai pakrera mrityudanda diiyo — kroosmaa taangera, tyas samayako sabaibhandaa kroor sajaaya. Tara yo sabai Parameshwarko yojanaabhitrai thiyo.','The next day he was arrested and executed — nailed to a cross, the cruelest punishment of that age. Yet all of it lay inside God’s plan.','Luke 23 · Acts 2:23'],
['क्रूसमा येशूले हाम्रो पाप आफैँमाथि लिनुभयो। उहाँ नै साँचो निस्तारको थुमा हुनुहुन्छ।','Kroosmaa Yeshule haamro paap aaphainmaathi linubhayo. Uhaan nai saancho nistaarko thumaa hunuhunchha.','On the cross Jesus took our sin upon himself. He is the true Passover Lamb.','Isaiah 53 · 1 Corinthians 5:7'],
['येशू मर्नुहुँदा मन्दिरको पर्दा माथिदेखि तलसम्म च्यातियो। परमेश्वरकहाँ जाने ढोका अब सबैका लागि खुला छ।','Yeshu marnuhundaa mandirko pardaa maathidekhi talasamma chyaatiyo. Parameshwarkahaan jaane dhokaa aba sabaikaa laagi khulaa chha.','When Jesus died, the temple curtain tore from top to bottom. The way into God’s presence now stands open to everyone.','Matthew 27:51'],
['तेस्रो दिन येशू मृत्युबाट जीवित हुनुभयो। मृत्यु पराजित भयो।','Tesro din Yeshu mrityubaata jeewit hunubhayo. Mrityu paraajit bhayo.','On the third day Jesus rose from the dead. Death itself was defeated.','Luke 24'],
['मानिसलाई आफ्नो पकडमा राख्ने अन्धकारका शक्तिहरूलाई पनि उहाँले त्यहीँ पराजित गर्नुभयो। हामीले न त तिनीहरूले नै बुझेका थिए — क्रूस त सुरुदेखिकै योजना थियो। त्यसैद्वारा हामी फेरि स्वतन्त्रतामा र परमेश्वरसँगको सम्बन्धमा हिँड्न सक्ने बाटो खुल्यो।','Maanislaai aaphno pakadmaa raakhne andhakaarkaa shaktiharulaai pani uhaanle tyahin paraajit garnubhayo. Haamile na ta tiniharule nai bujhekaa thie — kroos ta surudekhikai yojanaa thiyo. Tyasaidwaaraa haami pheri swatantrataamaa ra Parameshwarsangako sambandhamaa hindna sakne baato khulyo.','There he also defeated the dark powers that held humanity in their grip. Neither we nor they had understood: the cross was the plan from the very beginning. Through it the way opened for us to walk in freedom and relationship with God once again.','Colossians 2:15 · 1 Corinthians 2:8'],
['अब परमेश्वरकहाँ फर्कने बाटो खुल्यो। भाँचिएको सङ्गति फेरि जोडियो।','Aba Parameshwarkahaan pharkane baato khulyo. Bhaanchieko sangati pheri jodiyo.','Now the way back to God stands open. The broken fellowship is joined again.','Romans 5:1–11'],
['उहाँमा कुनै पाप थिएन — तर हाम्रो पाप उहाँले बोक्नुभयो, ताकि हामी परमेश्वरको अगाडि धर्मी ठहरिन सकौं। यो नै ठूलो साटासाट हो।','Uhaanmaa kunai paap thiena — tara haamro paap uhaanle boknubhayo, taaki haami Parameshwarko agaadi dharmi thaharina sakaun. Yo nai thulo saataasaat ho.','He had no sin of his own — yet he carried ours, so that we could stand righteous before God. This is the great exchange.','2 Corinthians 5:21']]},
{id:'newcreation',t:'New creation',ne:'नयाँ सृष्टि',art:FNE_ART.newcreation,
note:['कथा आत्माहरू कतै उडेर जाने गरी सिद्धिँदैन। नयाँ आकाश, नयाँ पृथ्वी, र आफ्ना मानिसहरूसँग बास गर्नुहुने परमेश्वर — बगैंचा फर्किन्छ, अझ राम्रो भएर। ढोका खुला छ।','Kathaa aatmaaharu katai udera jaane gari siddhindaina. Nayaan aakaash, nayaan prithvi, ra aaphnaa maanisharusanga baas garnuhune Parameshwar — bagainchaa pharkinchha, ajha raamro bhaera. Dhokaa khulaa chha.','The story does not end with souls floating away. It ends with heaven and earth made new, God at home with his people, the garden restored — better than the beginning. And the door is open.'],
paras:[
['जीवित हुनुभएपछि येशूले आफ्ना चेलाहरूलाई — अर्थात् उहाँलाई पछ्याउने साथीहरूलाई — पवित्र आत्मा दिनुभयो र संसारभरि पठाउनुभयो।','Jeewit hunubhaepachhi Yeshule aaphnaa chelaaharulaai — arthaat uhaanlaai pachhyaaune saathiharulaai — Pawitra Aatmaa dinubhayo ra sansaarbhari pathaunubhayo.','After he rose, Jesus gave his disciples — the friends who followed him — the Holy Spirit, and sent them out into all the world.','Acts 1–2'],
['पवित्र आत्मा भनेको परमेश्वर आफैँ हुनुहुन्छ — अब उहाँ आफ्ना मानिसहरूभित्र बास गर्नुहुन्छ, सान्त्वना दिनुहुन्छ, र बाटो देखाउनुहुन्छ।','Pawitra Aatmaa bhaneko Parameshwar aaphain hunuhunchha — aba uhaan aaphnaa maanisharubhitra baas garnuhunchha, saantwanaa dinuhunchha, ra baato dekhaunuhunchha.','The Holy Spirit is God himself — now making his home inside his people, comforting them and guiding the way.','John 14:16–17'],
['पहिले मानिसहरू परमेश्वरलाई भेट्न मन्दिर जान्थे। अब अचम्मको कुरा भएको छ — परमेश्वरको आत्मा पाएका उहाँका मानिसहरू नै उहाँको मन्दिर भएका छन्। हामी सँगै भेला भएर उहाँलाई आराधना गर्दा र एकअर्कालाई प्रेम गर्दा, परमेश्वर हामीभित्र र हाम्रै बीचमा बास गर्नुहुन्छ।','Pahile maanisharu Parameshwarlaai bhetna mandir jaanthe. Aba achammako kuraa bhaeko chha — Parameshwarko aatmaa paaekaa uhaankaa maanisharu nai uhaanko mandir bhaekaa chhan. Haami sangai bhelaa bhaera uhaanlaai aaraadhanaa gardaa ra ekarkaalaai prem gardaa, Parameshwar haamibhitra ra haamrai beechmaa baas garnuhunchha.','Before, people went to a temple to meet God. Now something astonishing has happened: God’s own people, filled with his Spirit, ARE his temple. As we gather to worship him and love one another, God dwells within us and among us.','1 Corinthians 3:16'],
['पहिलो विश्वासीहरू सँगै बस्थे — सँगै खान्थे, प्रार्थना गर्थे, र एकअर्कालाई सहायता गर्थे। संसारले भन्यो — हेर, तिनीहरूले कसरी प्रेम गर्छन्!','Pahilo vishwaasiharu sangai basthe — sangai khaanthe, praarthanaa garthe, ra ekarkaalaai sahaayataa garthe. Sansaarle bhanyo — hera, tiniharule kasari prem garchhan!','The first believers lived life together — eating, praying, helping one another. And the watching world said: see how they love!','Acts 2:42–47'],
['त्यो सुसमाचार संसारभरि फैलियो — र आज नेपालका हजारौं गाउँमा पनि येशूका चेलाहरू छन्। कथा अझै लेखिँदैछ।','Tyo susamaachaar sansaarbhari phailiyo — ra aaja Nepaalkaa hajaraun gaaunmaa pani Yeshukaa chelaaharu chhan. Kathaa ajhai lekhindaichha.','That good news spread across the world — and today there are followers of Jesus in thousands of villages of Nepal. The story is still being written.','Acts 1:8'],
['यो निम्तो इस्राएलमा मात्र रोकिएन — अब सबै जातिहरू परमेश्वरका मानिस बन्न बोलाइएका छन्। एशियाली, अफ्रिकी, पश्चिमी — हरेक जाति र भाषाका मानिसहरू एउटै परिवारमा, भक्ति, प्रेम र आज्ञापालनको जीवनमा येशूलाई सँगसँगै पछ्याउँछन्। येशूको जीवन, मृत्यु र पुनरुत्थानले संसार बदल्यो — एक-एक व्यक्ति गर्दै, हरेकलाई विश्वासयोग्य, दयालु र उदार सृष्टिकर्तासँगको सम्बन्धमा फर्काउँदै।','Yo nimto Israelmaa maatra rokiena — aba sabai jaatiharu Parameshwarkaa maanis banna bolaaiekaa chhan. Eshiyaali, Aphriki, pashchimi — harek jaati ra bhaashaakaa maanisharu eutai pariwaarmaa, bhakti, prem ra aagyaapaalanko jeewanmaa Yeshulaai sangasangai pachhyaunchhan. Yeshuko jeewan, mrityu ra punarutthaanle sansaar badalyo — ek-ek vyakti gardai, hareklaai vishwaasyogya, dayaalu ra udaar srishtikartaasangako sambandhamaa pharkaaundai.','And the invitation did not stop at Israel — now all nations are called to become the people of God. Asian, African, Western — people of every nation and language in one family, following Jesus together in a life of devotion, love and obedience. The life, death and resurrection of Jesus changed the world — one person at a time, each one brought back into relationship with a faithful, kind and generous Creator.','Galatians 3:28 · Revelation 7:9'],
['एक दिन येशू फेरि आउनुहुनेछ। परमेश्वरले नयाँ आकाश र नयाँ पृथ्वी बनाउनुहुनेछ।','Ek din Yeshu pheri aaunuhunechha. Parameshwarle nayaan aakaash ra nayaan prithvi banaunuhunechha.','One day Jesus will come again, and God will make a new heaven and a new earth.','Revelation 21:1'],
['त्यहाँ परमेश्वर आफ्ना मानिसहरूसँग बास गर्नुहुनेछ। न आँसु, न मृत्यु — सङ्गति सधैँको लागि।','Tyahaan Parameshwar aaphnaa maanisharusanga baas garnuhunechha. Na aansu, na mrityu — sangati sadhainko laagi.','There God will dwell with his people. No more tears, no more death — fellowship forever.','Revelation 21:3–4'],
['यो कथा तपाईंको पनि हुन सक्छ। येशूमा विश्वास गर्नुहोस्, र घर फर्कनुहोस्।','Yo kathaa tapaainko pani huna sakchha. Yeshumaa vishwaas garnuhos, ra ghar pharkanuhos.','This story can be yours too. Believe in Jesus, and come home.','John 3:16']]}
]},

{id:'fjesus',title:'Jesus',ne:'येशू',
overview:{t:'Who is Jesus?',ne:'येशू को हुनुहुन्छ?',art:FNE_ART.ovjesus,
start:['सुरुदेखि हेरौं','From here — his story in detail'],
paras:[
['येशू परमेश्वरका पुत्र हुनुहुन्छ — परमेश्वर आफैँ, हामीजस्तै मानिस बन्नुभयो।','Yeshu Parameshwarkaa putra hunuhunchha — Parameshwar aaphain, haamijastai maanis bannubhayo.','Jesus is the Son of God — God himself, become human like us.','John 1:1,14'],
['उहाँ हामीजस्तै जिउनुभयो — तर पापविना — र आफ्नो जीवनले परमेश्वरको प्रेम देखाउनुभयो।','Uhaan haamijastai jiunubhayo — tara paapwinaa — ra aaphno jeewanle Parameshwarko prem dekhaunubhayo.','He lived as we live — yet without sin — and his whole life showed us the love of God.','Hebrews 4:15'],
['उहाँले आफ्नो ज्यान हाम्रा लागि दिनुभयो र मृत्युलाई जित्नुभयो।','Uhaanle aaphno jyaan haamraa laagi dinubhayo ra mrityulaai jitnubhayo.','He laid down his life for us — and he defeated death.','John 10:11 · Luke 24'],
['आज पनि उहाँ जीवित हुनुहुन्छ र हरेकलाई बोलाउनुहुन्छ — मकहाँ आओ।','Aaja pani uhaan jeewit hunuhunchha ra hareklaai bolaunuhunchha — makahaan aao.','He is alive today, and he calls every person: come to me.','Matthew 11:28'],
['उहाँको बारेमा जान्नु मात्र होइन — उहाँलाई चिन्नु। तलका कथाहरू त्यही निम्तो हुन्।','Uhaanko baaremaa jaannu maatra hoina — uhaanlaai chinnu. Talakaa kathaaharu tyahi nimto hun.','The goal is not just to know about him — it is to know him. The stories below are that invitation.','John 17:3'],
['अब यहाँबाट हामी उहाँको कथा सुरुदेखि हेर्नेछौं — जन्मदेखि रित्तो चिहानसम्म, एक-एक घटना गरेर।','Aba yahaanbaata haami uhaanko kathaa surudekhi hernechhaun — janmadekhi ritto chihaansamma, ek-ek ghatanaa garera.','From here, we will walk through his story from the beginning — from his birth to the empty tomb, one moment at a time.']]},
sections:[
{id:'jbirth',t:'The birth',ne:'जन्म',art:FNE_ART.jbirth,
note:['सबै थोकका राजा दरबारविना, तुरहीविना आउनुभयो। पहिलो साक्षीको रूपमा परमेश्वरले गोठालाहरूलाई रोज्नुभयो — यो राज्य पहिलो रातदेखि नै यसरी चल्छ।','Sabai thokkaa raajaa darbaarwinaa, turahiwinaa aaunubhayo. Pahilo saakshiko rupmaa Parameshwarle gothaalaaharulaai rojnubhayo — yo raajya pahilo raatdekhi nai yasari chalchha.','The King of everything arrived with no palace and no trumpet — and God chose shepherds as the first witnesses. That is how this kingdom works from its very first night.'],
paras:[
['येशू जन्मनुभन्दा सयौं वर्षअघि नै इस्राएलका अगमवक्ताहरूले एक जना आउनुहुनेको बारेमा बताएका थिए — तिनीहरूले उहाँलाई आउनुहुने मसीह भनेर चिने। तिनीहरूले उहाँलाई धेरै नाम दिए — अचम्मको सल्लाहकार, शक्तिशाली परमेश्वर, अनन्तका पिता, शान्तिका राजकुमार — र उहाँ कन्याबाट जन्मनुहुनेछ भनेर लेखे। त्यही भविष्यवाणी अब पूरा हुन लागेको थियो।','Yeshu janmanubhandaa sayaun barshaaghi nai Israelkaa agamwaktaaharule ek janaa aaunuhuneko baaremaa bataaekaa thie — tiniharule uhaanlaai aaunuhune Maseeh bhanera chine. Tiniharule uhaanlaai dherai naam die — achammako sallaahakaar, shaktishaali Parameshwar, anantakaa Pitaa, shaantikaa raajkumaar — ra uhaan kanyaabaata janmanuhunechha bhanera lekhe. Tyahi bhavishyavaani aba puraa huna laageko thiyo.','Hundreds of years before Jesus was born, the prophets of Israel told of someone who would come — they knew him as the coming Messiah. They gave him many names — Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace — and they wrote that he would be born of a virgin. Now that prophecy was about to come true.','Isaiah 9:6 · 7:14'],
['गब्रिएल स्वर्गदूतले मरियमलाई भने — तिमीले एउटा छोरो जन्माउनेछ्यौ, र उहाँको नाम येशू राख्नू।','Gabriel swargadootle Mariyamlaai bhane — timile eutaa chhoro janmaunechhyau, ra uhaanko naam Yeshu raakhnu.','The angel Gabriel told Mary: you will have a son, and you are to name him Jesus.','Luke 1:26–33'],
['मरियम कुनै रानी थिइनन् — नासरत गाउँकी एउटी साधारण युवती। परमेश्वरले ठूला कामका लागि साधारण मानिसहरूलाई नै रोज्नुहुन्छ।','Mariyam kunai raani thiinan — Naasarat gaaunki eutii saadhaaran yuwati. Parameshwarle thulaa kaamkaa laagi saadhaaran maanisharulaai nai rojnuhunchha.','Mary was no queen — just an ordinary young woman from the village of Nazareth. God loves to choose ordinary people for his greatest work.','Luke 1:26–38'],
['येशू बेथलेहेममा जन्मनुभयो — सानो गाउँ, सानो डुँड। गोठालाहरू पहिलो पाहुना भए।','Yeshu Bethlehemmaa janmanubhayo — saano gaaun, saano dund. Gothaalaaharu pahilo paahunaa bhae.','Jesus was born in Bethlehem — a small town, a humble manger. Shepherds were the first visitors.','Luke 2'],
['टाढा पूर्वबाट ज्योतिषीहरू तारा पछ्याउँदै आए। तिनीहरूले बालकलाई दण्डवत् गरे र बहुमूल्य उपहारहरू चढाए।','Taadhaa purbabaata jyotishiharu taaraa pachhyaaundai aae. Tiniharule baalaklaai dandawat gare ra bahumulya upahaarharu chadhaae.','From the far east, wise men came following a star. They bowed before the child and offered him precious gifts.','Matthew 2:1–11'],
['येशू नामको अर्थ यही हो — उहाँले आफ्ना मानिसहरूलाई तिनीहरूका पापबाट बचाउनुहुनेछ।','Yeshu naamko artha yahi ho — uhaanle aaphnaa maanisharulaai tiniharukaa paapbaata bachaunuhunechha.','The name Jesus carries his mission: he will save his people from their sins.','Matthew 1:21'],
['त्यो रात आकाश स्वर्गदूतहरूले भरियो — सबैभन्दा उच्चमा परमेश्वरलाई महिमा, र पृथ्वीमा शान्ति!','Tyo raat aakaash swargadootharule bhariyo — sabaibhandaa uchchamaa Parameshwarlaai mahimaa, ra prithvimaa shaanti!','That night the sky filled with angels: glory to God in the highest — and on earth, peace!','Luke 2:13–14']]},
{id:'jbaptism',t:'Baptism and the wilderness',ne:'बप्तिस्मा र उजाडस्थान',art:FNE_ART.jbaptism,
note:['येशू हामी उभिने ठाउँमा उभिनुभयो — पापीहरूसँगै पानीमा। अनि हामी लड्ने ठाउँमा दह्रो उभिनुभयो — आदम र इस्राएल असफल भएका हरेक ठाउँमा उहाँले जित्नुभयो।','Yeshu haami ubhine thaaunmaa ubhinubhayo — paapiharusangai paanimaa. Ani haami ladne thaaunmaa dahro ubhinubhayo — Aadam ra Israel asaphal bhaekaa harek thaaunmaa uhaanle jitnubhayo.','Jesus stands where we stand — in the water alongside sinners — and stands firm where we fall, winning in every place Adam and Israel failed.'],
paras:[
['यूहन्ना नदीको छेउमा बसेर मानिसहरूलाई बोलाउँथे — पाप छोडेर परमेश्वरतिर फर्क! नयाँ सुरुवातको चिन्हको रूपमा उनले फर्कनेहरूलाई पानीमा डुबाउँथे — त्यसैलाई बप्तिस्मा भनिन्छ।','Yuhannaa nadiko chheumaa basera maanisharulaai bolaunthe — paap chhodera Parameshwartira pharka! Nayaan suruwaatko chinhako rupmaa unle pharkaneharulaai paanimaa dubaunthe — tyasailaai baptismaa bhaninchha.','John lived by the river, calling people: turn from sin, back to God! As a sign of that new start he would dip the returning ones in the water — that is what baptism means.','Matthew 3:1–6'],
['यूहन्नाले येशूलाई नदीमा बप्तिस्मा दिए। आकाशबाट आवाज आयो — यिनी मेरा प्रिय पुत्र हुन्।','Yuhannaale Yeshulaai nadeemaa baptismaa die. Aakaashbaata aawaaj aayo — yini meraa priya putra hun.','John baptized Jesus in the river, and a voice came from heaven: this is my beloved Son.','Matthew 3:13–17'],
['उजाडस्थानमा शैतानले येशूलाई परीक्षा गर्यो। तर आदमजस्तो होइन — येशूले जित्नुभयो।','Ujaadsthaanmaa shaitaanle Yeshulaai parikshaa garyo. Tara Aadamjasto hoina — Yeshule jitnubhayo.','In the wilderness Satan tested Jesus. But where Adam fell, Jesus stood firm and won.','Matthew 4:1–11'],
['त्यसपछि येशूले साधारण मानिसहरूलाई बोलाउनुभयो — जालहरू छोडेर तिनीहरू उहाँको पछि लागे। बाह्र जना चेला बने।','Tyaspachhi Yeshule saadhaaran maanisharulaai bolaunubhayo — jaalharu chhodera tiniharu uhaanko pachhi laage. Baahra janaa chelaa bane.','Then Jesus called ordinary people — they left their fishing nets and followed him. Twelve became his disciples.','Mark 1:16–20'],
['चालीस दिनसम्म येशूले केही खानुभएन। हरेक परीक्षाको जवाफ उहाँले परमेश्वरको वचनले दिनुभयो — लेखिएको छ।','Chaalis dinsamma Yeshule kehi khaanubhaena. Harek parikshaako jawaaph uhaanle Parameshwarko wachanle dinubhayo — lekhieko chha.','For forty days Jesus ate nothing. And he answered every temptation with the word of God: it is written.','Matthew 4:2–10']]},
{id:'jkingdom',t:'The kingdom announced',ne:'राज्यको सुसमाचार',art:FNE_ART.jkingdom,
note:['परमेश्वरको राज्य नक्साको कुनै ठाउँ होइन — माटो फोरेर उम्रने बीउजस्तै संसारभित्र पस्ने उहाँको असल शासन हो। र त्यसको ढोका पहिले सबैभन्दा असम्भावित मानिसहरूका लागि खुल्छ।','Parameshwarko raajya naksaako kunai thaaun hoina — maato phorera umrane biujastai sansaarbhitra pasne uhaanko asal shaasan ho. Ra tyasko dhokaa pahile sabaibhandaa asambhaawit maanisharukaa laagi khulchha.','The kingdom of God is not a place on a map — it is God’s own good rule breaking in, quiet as a seed pushing up through soil. And its door opens first to the least likely people.'],
paras:[
['येशूले भन्नुभयो — परमेश्वरको राज्य नजिकै आएको छ। फर्केर आओ र सुसमाचारमा विश्वास गर।','Yeshule bhannubhayo — Parameshwarko raajya najikai aaeko chha. Pharkera aau ra susamaachaarmaa vishwaas gara.','Jesus announced: the kingdom of God has come near. Turn around, and believe the good news.','Mark 1:15'],
['उहाँले गरिबहरूलाई, बिरामीहरूलाई र पापीहरूलाई नजिक बोलाउनुभयो।','Uhaanle garibharulaai, biraamiharulaai ra paapiharulaai najik bolaunubhayo.','He called the poor, the sick and the sinners near — the very people others pushed away.','Luke 5:27–32'],
['डाँडामा बसेर उहाँले सिकाउनुभयो — धन्य हुन् आत्मामा गरिब हुनेहरू, किनभने स्वर्गको राज्य तिनीहरूकै हो। धन्य हुन् नम्रहरू। धन्य हुन् शान्ति गराउनेहरू। संसारले जसलाई तल देख्छ, परमेश्वरले तिनीहरूलाई धन्य भन्नुहुन्छ।','Daandaamaa basera uhaanle sikaunubhayo — dhanya hun aatmaamaa garib huneharu, kinabhane swargako raajya tiniharukai ho. Dhanya hun namraharu. Dhanya hun shaanti garaauneharu. Sansaarle jaslaai tala dekhchha, Parameshwarle tiniharulaai dhanya bhannuhunchha.','Sitting on a hillside he taught: blessed are the poor in spirit, for the kingdom of heaven is theirs. Blessed are the humble. Blessed are the peacemakers. The very people the world looks down on, God calls blessed.','Matthew 5:3–9'],
['मानिसहरूले साना बालबालिकालाई येशूकहाँ ल्याए। चेलाहरूले तिनीहरूलाई रोके — तर येशूले भन्नुभयो — बालबालिकालाई मकहाँ आउन देऊ, नरोक। परमेश्वरको राज्य यस्तैहरूको हो।','Maanisharule saanaa baalbaalikaalaai Yeshukahaan lyaae. Chelaaharule tiniharulaai roke — tara Yeshule bhannubhayo — baalbaalikaalaai makahaan aauna deu, naroka. Parameshwarko raajya yastaiharuko ho.','People brought little children to Jesus. His disciples turned them away — but Jesus said: let the children come to me, do not stop them. The kingdom of God belongs to such as these.','Mark 10:13–14'],
['राज्य खेतमा लुकेको धनजस्तै हो — भेट्टाउने मानिसले खुशीले आफ्नो सबै थोक बेचेर त्यो खेत किन्छ।','Raajya khetmaa lukeko dhanjastai ho — bhettaaune maanisle khushile aaphno sabai thok bechera tyo khet kinchha.','The kingdom is like treasure hidden in a field: the one who finds it joyfully sells everything to buy that field.','Matthew 13:44'],
['येशूले भन्नुभयो — परमेश्वरको राज्य रायोको गेडाजस्तै हो। सबैभन्दा सानो बीउ, तर बढेर ठूलो रूख बन्छ, र चराहरूले त्यसका हाँगामा गुँड बनाउँछन्।','Yeshule bhannubhayo — Parameshwarko raajya raayoko gedaajastai ho. Sabaibhandaa saano biu, tara badhera thulo rukh banchha, ra charaaharule tyaskaa haangaamaa gund banaunchhan.','Jesus said: the kingdom of God is like a mustard seed — the smallest of seeds, yet it grows into a great tree, and the birds nest in its branches.','Mark 4:30–32']]},
{id:'jprayer',t:'Jesus teaches prayer',ne:'प्रार्थना',art:FNE_ART.jprayer,
note:['प्रार्थनाको पहिलो शब्दले नै सबै भन्छ — पिता। हामी राजाको दरबारमा होइन, बुबाको काखमा आउँछौं। त्यही ढोका येशूले खोलिदिनुभयो।','Praarthanaako pahilo shabdale nai sabai bhanchha — Pitaa. Haami raajaako darbaarmaa hoina, bubaako kaakhmaa aaunchhaun. Tyahi dhokaa Yeshule kholidinubhayo.','The first word of the prayer says it all — Father. We come not into a king’s court but onto a father’s lap. That is the door Jesus opened.'],
paras:[
['येशू बिहान सबेरै एक्लै प्रार्थना गर्न जानुहुन्थ्यो। चेलाहरूले भने — प्रभु, हामीलाई पनि प्रार्थना गर्न सिकाउनुहोस्।','Yeshu bihaana saberai eklai praarthanaa garna jaanuhunthyo. Chelaaharule bhane — Prabhu, haamilaai pani praarthanaa garna sikaunuhos.','Jesus would go out early in the morning to pray alone. His followers asked: Lord, teach us to pray too.','Mark 1:35 · Luke 11:1'],
['उहाँले सिकाउनुभयो — यसरी प्रार्थना गर: हे हाम्रा स्वर्गीय पिता, तपाईंको नाम पवित्र मानियोस्। तपाईंको राज्य आओस्।','Uhaanle sikaunubhayo — yasari praarthanaa gara: he haamraa swargiya Pitaa, tapaainko naam pawitra maaniyos. Tapaainko raajya aaos.','He taught them: pray like this — our Father in heaven, may your name be honored as holy, may your kingdom come.','Matthew 6:9–10'],
['हामीलाई आजको रोटी दिनुहोस्। हाम्रा पाप क्षमा गर्नुहोस्, जसरी हामीले पनि अरूलाई क्षमा गरेका छौं।','Haamilaai aajako roti dinuhos. Haamraa paap kshamaa garnuhos, jasari haamile pani arulaai kshamaa garekaa chhaun.','Give us today the food we need. Forgive our sins, as we also forgive those who wrong us.','Matthew 6:11–12'],
['हामीलाई परीक्षामा पर्न नदिनुहोस्, तर दुष्टबाट छुटाउनुहोस्। — यति सरल, यति गहिरो। यही प्रार्थना आज पनि संसारभरि येशूका चेलाहरूले गर्छन्।','Haamilaai parikshaamaa parna nadinuhos, tara dushtabaata chhutaaunuhos. — Yati saral, yati gahiro. Yahi praarthanaa aaja pani sansaarbhari Yeshukaa chelaaharule garchhan.','And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil. So simple, so deep. Followers of Jesus around the world still pray this prayer today.','Matthew 6:13'],
['प्रार्थना भनेको लामो भाषण होइन — बुबासँग कुरा गर्नु हो। परमेश्वरले सुन्नुहुन्छ।','Praarthanaa bhaneko laamo bhaashan hoina — bubaasanga kuraa garnu ho. Parameshwarle sunnuhunchha.','Prayer is not a long speech — it is talking with your Father. And God listens.','Matthew 6:7–8'],
['येशूले भन्नुभयो — माग, र तिमीलाई दिइनेछ। खोज, र तिमीले भेट्टाउनेछौ। ढकढक्याऊ, र ढोका खोलिनेछ।','Yeshule bhannubhayo — maaga, ra timilaai diinechha. Khoja, ra timile bhettaaunechhau. Dhakdhakyaau, ra dhokaa kholinechha.','Jesus said: ask, and it will be given to you. Seek, and you will find. Knock, and the door will be opened.','Matthew 7:7']]},
{id:'jmiracles',t:'Power and compassion',ne:'शक्ति र दया',art:FNE_ART.jmiracles,
note:['चमत्कारहरू जादु होइनन् — झलकहरू हुन्। हरेक चङ्गाइ, शान्त भएको आँधी, बढेको रोटी — रोग, भोक र डर नभएको संसारको झ्याल हो।','Chamatkaarharu jaadu hoinan — jhalakharu hun. Harek changaai, shaanta bhaeko aandhi, badheko roti — rog, bhok ra dar nabhaeko sansaarko jhyaal ho.','The miracles are not magic — they are previews. Every healing, every calmed storm, every multiplied loaf is a window into the world as God intends it.'],
paras:[
['येशूले बिरामीलाई निको पार्नुभयो र अन्धालाई देख्ने बनाउनुभयो।','Yeshule biraamilaai niko paarnubhayo ra andhaalaai dekhne banaunubhayo.','Jesus healed the sick and gave the blind their sight.','Matthew 9'],
['एक जना कुष्ठरोगी येशूकहाँ आयो — जसलाई कसैले छुँदैनथ्यो। येशूले हात पसारेर उसलाई छुनुभयो र भन्नुभयो — निको होऊ।','Ek janaa kushtharogi Yeshukahaan aayo — jaslaai kasaile chhundainathyo. Yeshule haat pasaarera uslaai chhunubhayo ra bhannubhayo — niko hou.','A man with leprosy came to Jesus — a man nobody would touch. Jesus reached out his hand, touched him, and said: be healed.','Mark 1:40–42'],
['उहाँले आँधीलाई शान्त पार्नुभयो। चेलाहरूले सोधे — यिनी को हुन्?','Uhaanle aandhilaai shaanta paarnubhayo. Chelaaharule sodhe — yini ko hun?','He calmed a storm with a word. His disciples asked each other: who IS this?','Mark 4:35–41'],
['पाँचवटा रोटी र दुईवटा माछाले उहाँले हजारौंलाई खुवाउनुभयो।','Paanchwataa roti ra duiwataa maachhaale uhaanle hajaraunlaai khuwaunubhayo.','With five loaves and two fish he fed thousands.','John 6:1–14'],
['मरेकी एउटी सानी छोरीको हात समातेर उहाँले भन्नुभयो — छोरी, उठ। र त्यो केटी उठिन्। मृत्यु पनि उहाँको वचन मान्छ।','Marekii eutii saani chhoriko haat samaatera uhaanle bhannubhayo — chhori, utha. Ra tyo keti uthin. Mrityu pani uhaanko wachan maanchha.','Taking the hand of a little girl who had died, he said: child, get up. And she rose. Even death obeys his word.','Mark 5:41–42'],
['उहाँ साधारण मानिसहरूसँग हिँड्नुभयो — माछा मार्नेहरू, पापी भनिएकाहरू, भाँचिएका र बिरामीहरू — र उहाँले तिनीहरूलाई निको पार्नुभयो। भाँचिएका हामीप्रति परमेश्वरको कति गहिरो प्रेम र दया छ भनेर उहाँले नै देखाइदिनुभयो।','Uhaan saadhaaran maanisharusanga hindnubhayo — maachhaa maarneharu, paapi bhaniekaaharu, bhaanchiekaa ra biraamiharu — ra uhaanle tiniharulaai niko paarnubhayo. Bhaanchiekaa haamiprati Parameshwarko kati gahiro prem ra dayaa chha bhanera uhaanle nai dekhaaidinubhayo.','He walked with ordinary people — fishermen, so-called sinners, the broken and the sick — and he made them well. He showed us how deep the love and kindness of God is for us as broken people.','Matthew 9:35–36']]},
{id:'jlostson',t:'The lost son',ne:'हराएको छोरा',art:FNE_ART.jlostson,
note:['दौडिने बुबा नै यस कथाको केन्द्र हो — त्यो संस्कृतिमा इज्जतदार मानिस कहिल्यै दौडिँदैनथे। फर्कने छोरालाई अँगाल्न परमेश्वर आफ्नो इज्जत पनि हेर्नुहुन्न।','Daudine bubaa nai yas kathaako kendra ho — tyo sanskritimaa ijjatdaar maanis kahilyai daudindainathe. Pharkane chhoraalaai angaalna Parameshwar aaphno ijjat pani hernuhunna.','The father RUNNING is the center of this parable — in that culture a dignified man never ran. God sets aside his own dignity to embrace the child who comes home.'],
paras:[
['धार्मिक मानिसहरूले येशूको बारेमा गनगन गरे — यो मानिसले त पापीहरूलाई ग्रहण गर्छ, तिनीहरूसँगै खान्छ! जवाफमा येशूले यो कथा भन्नुभयो — एउटा छोराले बुबाको सम्पत्ति लिएर टाढा गयो र सबै उडायो।','Dhaarmik maanisharule Yeshuko baaremaa gangan gare — yo maanisle ta paapiharulaai grahan garchha, tiniharusangai khaanchha! Jawaaphmaa Yeshule yo kathaa bhannubhayo — eutaa chhoraale bubaako sampatti liera taadhaa gayo ra sabai udaayo.','The religious people grumbled about Jesus: this man welcomes sinners — he even eats with them! In answer, Jesus told this story. A son took his father’s wealth, went far away, and wasted it all.','Luke 15:1–2 · 11–16'],
['टाढा देशमा छोरो यति भोकायो कि सुँगुरको दाना पनि खान तयार भयो। अनि उसले सम्झ्यो — बुबाको घरमा त नोकरहरूले पनि पेटभरि खान्छन्। म फर्किन्छु।','Taadhaa deshmaa chhoro yati bhokaayo ki sungurko daanaa pani khaana tayaar bhayo. Ani usle samjhyo — bubaako gharmaa ta nokarharule pani petbhari khaanchhan. Ma pharkinchhu.','In the far country the son grew so hungry he was ready to eat the pigs’ food. Then he came to his senses: even my father’s servants eat their fill. I will go home.','Luke 15:14–19'],
['छोरो घर फर्कंदा बुबा दौडेर आए र अँगालो हाले।','Chhoro ghar pharkandaa bubaa daudera aae ra angaalo haale.','When the son came home, the father RAN to him and threw his arms around him.','Luke 15:20–24'],
['परमेश्वरको हृदय त्यस्तै छ — फर्कने हरेकलाई उहाँले खुशीसाथ ग्रहण गर्नुहुन्छ।','Parameshwarko hridaya tyastai chha — pharkane hareklaai uhaanle khushisaath grahan garnuhunchha.','That is the heart of God: he joyfully welcomes everyone who comes home.','Luke 15'],
['जेठो छोरो भने रिसायो — म त वर्षौंदेखि तपाईंको सेवा गर्दैछु! बुबाले भने — छोरा, मेरो जे छ, सबै तिम्रै हो। तर तिम्रो भाइ हराएको थियो, अहिले भेट्टाइयो — रमाउनु त पर्छ नि।','Jetho chhoro bhane risaayo — ma ta barshaundekhi tapaainko sewaa gardaichhu! Bubaale bhane — chhoraa, mero je chha, sabai timrai ho. Tara timro bhaai haraaeko thiyo, ahile bhettaaiyo — ramaaunu ta parchha ni.','But the elder son was angry: all these years I have served you! The father said: son, everything I have is yours. But your brother was lost and is found — how could we not celebrate?','Luke 15:25–32']]},
{id:'jsamaritan',t:'The good Samaritan',ne:'असल सामरी',art:FNE_ART.jsamaritan,
note:['येशूले प्रश्न नै उल्टाइदिनुभयो। मेरो प्रेम कसले पाउन योग्य छ होइन — म कसरी असल छिमेकी बन्न सक्छु? अनि उहाँले बाहिरको मानिसलाई नै कथाको नायक बनाउनुभयो।','Yeshule prashna nai ultaaidinubhayo. Mero prem kasle paauna yogya chha hoina — ma kasari asal chhimeki banna sakchhu? Ani uhaanle baahirako maanislaai nai kathaako naayak banaunubhayo.','Jesus flips the question. Not WHO deserves my love — but how can I BE a neighbor? And he makes the outsider the hero of the story.'],
paras:[
['कसैले सोध्यो — मेरो छिमेकी को हो? येशूले कथाले जवाफ दिनुभयो।','Kasaile sodhyo — mero chhimeki ko ho? Yeshule kathaale jawaaph dinubhayo.','Someone asked Jesus: who is my neighbor? He answered with a story.','Luke 10:25–29'],
['यरूशलेमबाट यरीहो जाने बाटो डरलाग्दो थियो — डाँकूहरूले एक जना यात्रुलाई कुटेर, लुटेर आधा मरेको छोडेका थिए।','Yarushalembaata Yariho jaane baato darlaagdo thiyo — daankuharule ek janaa yaatrulaai kutera, lutera aadhaa mareko chhodekaa thie.','The road from Jerusalem down to Jericho was dangerous — robbers had beaten a traveler and left him half dead.','Luke 10:30'],
['एउटा कुरा बुझ्नुपर्छ — त्यस बेला यहूदीहरू र सामरीहरू एकअर्कालाई घृणा गर्थे। सुन्नेहरूका लागि सामरी भनेको शत्रु थियो।','Eutaa kuraa bujhnuparchha — tyas belaa Yahudiharu ra Saamariharu ekarkaalaai ghrinaa garthe. Sunneharukaa laagi Saamari bhaneko shatru thiyo.','One thing to understand: in those days Jews and Samaritans despised each other. To the listeners, a Samaritan meant an enemy.','John 4:9'],
['बाटोमा घाइते मानिसलाई धर्मगुरुहरूले छोडे। तर एक जना सामरीले रोकिएर उसको हेरचाह गरे।','Baatomaa ghaaite maanislaai dharmaguruharule chhode. Tara ek janaa Saamarile rokiera usko herchaah gare.','Religious leaders passed the wounded man by. But a Samaritan — an outsider — stopped and cared for him.','Luke 10:30–35'],
['सामरीले घाउमा तेल र दाखमद्य लगाइदिए, उसलाई आफ्नै गधामा राखेर पौवामा लगे, र खर्च पनि तिरिदिए — फर्किंदा अरू लाग्यो भने म तिर्छु।','Saamarile ghaaumaa tel ra daakhmadhya lagaaidie, uslaai aaphnai gadhaamaa raakhera pauwaamaa lage, ra kharcha pani tiridie — pharkindaa aru laagyo bhane ma tirchhu.','He poured oil and wine on the wounds, set the man on his own donkey, brought him to an inn — and paid, promising: whatever more it costs, I will repay.','Luke 10:34–35'],
['येशूले भन्नुभयो — जाओ, तिमी पनि त्यस्तै गर।','Yeshule bhannubhayo — jaao, timi pani tyastai gara.','Jesus said: go and do the same.','Luke 10:37']]},
{id:'jbuilders',t:'The two builders',ne:'दुई घर बनाउनेहरू',art:FNE_ART.jbuilders,
note:['आफ्नो ठूलो उपदेशको अन्त्यमा येशूले सोध्नुहुन्छ — तिम्रो जीवनको जग के हो? सुन्नु राम्रो हो; गर्नु नै चट्टान हो।','Aaphno thulo updeshako antyamaa Yeshule sodhnuhunchha — timro jeewanko jag ke ho? Sunnu raamro ho; garnu nai chattaan ho.','Jesus ends his great sermon with a question: what is your life built on? Hearing is good — doing is the rock.'],
paras:[
['येशूले भन्नुभयो — मेरो वचन सुनेर पालन गर्ने मानिस चट्टानमाथि घर बनाउने बुद्धिमान् मानिसजस्तै हो।','Yeshule bhannubhayo — mero wachan sunera paalan garne maanis chattaanmaathi ghar banaaune buddhimaan maanisjastai ho.','Jesus said: whoever hears my words and does them is like a wise man who built his house on the rock.','Matthew 7:24'],
['वर्षा आयो, बाढी आयो, हुरी चल्यो — तर त्यो घर ढलेन, किनकि त्यसको जग चट्टानमाथि थियो।','Warshaa aayo, baadhi aayo, huri chalyo — tara tyo ghar dhalena, kinaki tyasko jag chattaanmaathi thiyo.','The rain came, the floods rose, the winds blew — but that house did not fall, because its foundation was on the rock.','Matthew 7:25'],
['तर सुनेर पनि नगर्ने मानिस बालुवामा घर बनाउने मूर्खजस्तै हो — हुरी आउँदा त्यो घर ठूलो गर्जनसँगै ढल्यो।','Tara sunera pani nagarne maanis baaluwaamaa ghar banaaune murkhajastai ho — huri aaundaa tyo ghar thulo garjansangai dhalyo.','But the one who hears and does not act is like a fool who built on sand — when the storm came, that house fell with a great crash.','Matthew 7:26–27'],
['यी दुई घर बाहिरबाट उस्तै देखिन्थे। फरक देखियो — आँधी आएपछि मात्र। जग परीक्षामा मात्र देखिन्छ।','Yi dui ghar baahirbaata ustai dekhinthe. Pharak dekhiyo — aandhi aaepachhi maatra. Jag parikshaamaa maatra dekhinchha.','From the outside the two houses looked the same. The difference showed only when the storm came. Foundations are revealed by testing.','Matthew 7 (the close)']]},
{id:'jcross',t:'The cross',ne:'क्रूस',art:FNE_ART.jcross,
note:['क्रूस येशूको सेवामा आइपरेको दुर्घटना थिएन — त्यो नै उहाँको सेवा थियो। कसैले उहाँको ज्यान खोसेन; उहाँले आफैँ दिनुभयो — प्रेमले पूरा मोल खुशीसाथ तिर्यो।','Kroos Yeshuko sewaamaa aaipareko durghatanaa thiena — tyo nai uhaanko sewaa thiyo. Kasaile uhaanko jyaan khosena; uhaanle aaphain dinubhayo — premle puraa mol khushisaath tiryo.','The cross was not an accident that interrupted Jesus’ mission — it WAS the mission. Nobody took his life; he laid it down, love paying the full price willingly.'],
paras:[
['आफ्ना साथीहरूका लागि ज्यान दिनुभन्दा ठूलो प्रेम अरू छैन — अनि येशूले त्यही गर्नुभयो।','Aaphnaa saathiharukaa laagi jyaan dinubhandaa thulo prem aru chhaina — ani Yeshule tyahi garnubhayo.','There is no greater love than to lay down your life for your friends — and that is exactly what Jesus did.','John 15:13'],
['धार्मिक अगुवाहरूको डाहले उहाँलाई मृत्युसम्म पुर्यायो। तर येशूले भन्नुभएको थियो — कसैले मेरो ज्यान खोस्दैन; म आफैँ दिन्छु।','Dhaarmik aguwaaharuko daahale uhaanlaai mrityusamma puryaayo. Tara Yeshule bhannubhaeko thiyo — kasaile mero jyaan khosdaina; ma aaphain dinchhu.','The envy of the religious leaders drove him to his death. But Jesus had already said: no one takes my life from me — I lay it down myself.','Matthew 27:18 · John 10:18'],
['क्रूसमा उहाँले प्रार्थना गर्नुभयो — पिता, यिनीहरूलाई क्षमा गर्नुहोस्।','Kroosmaa uhaanle praarthanaa garnubhayo — Pitaa, yiniharulaai kshamaa garnuhos.','From the cross he prayed: Father, forgive them.','Luke 23:34'],
['मध्यदिनमा तीन घण्टासम्म अन्धकार छायो। हाम्रो पापको सारा भार उहाँमाथि थियो।','Madhyadinmaa tin ghantaasamma andhakaar chhaayo. Haamro paapko saaraa bhaar uhaanmaathi thiyo.','At midday, darkness covered the land for three hours. The whole weight of our sin was upon him.','Matthew 27:45'],
['उहाँ पिताको प्रेम र राज्य प्रकट गर्न आउनुभएको थियो — तैपनि हामीले उहाँलाई इन्कार गर्यौं; मानिसहरूले नै उहाँलाई मारे। तर हामीलाई पनि, हामीले सेवा गर्ने अन्धकारका शक्तिहरूलाई पनि थाहा थिएन — यो त सुरुदेखिकै योजनाको हिस्सा थियो। येशूको मृत्युद्वारा नै परमेश्वरको राज्य स्वर्गमा जस्तै पृथ्वीमा पनि आउँदै थियो।','Uhaan Pitaako prem ra raajya prakat garna aaunubhaeko thiyo — taipani haamile uhaanlaai inkaar garyaun; maanisharule nai uhaanlaai maare. Tara haamilaai pani, haamile sewaa garne andhakaarkaa shaktiharulaai pani thaahaa thiena — yo ta surudekhikai yojanaako hissaa thiyo. Yeshuko mrityudwaaraa nai Parameshwarko raajya swargamaa jastai prithvimaa pani aaundai thiyo.','He had come to reveal the Father’s love and kingdom — yet we rejected him; human beings killed him. But neither we nor the dark forces we obeyed knew this was part of the plan all along. Through Jesus’ death, God’s kingdom was coming on earth as it is in heaven.','Acts 2:23 · 1 Corinthians 2:8'],
['येशूको छेउमा दुई जना डाँकू पनि झुण्ड्याइएका थिए। एउटाले भन्यो — येशू, तपाईं आफ्नो राज्यमा आउनुहुँदा मलाई सम्झनुहोस्। येशूले भन्नुभयो — आजै तिमी मसँग स्वर्गलोकमा हुनेछौ।','Yeshuko chheumaa dui janaa daanku pani jhundyaaiekaa thie. Eutaale bhanyo — Yeshu, tapaain aaphno raajyamaa aaunuhundaa malaai samjhanuhos. Yeshule bhannubhayo — aajai timi masanga swargalokmaa hunechhau.','Two criminals hung beside Jesus. One said: Jesus, remember me when you come into your kingdom. Jesus answered: today you will be with me in paradise.','Luke 23:39–43'],
['उहाँले भन्नुभयो — सिद्धियो। हाम्रो पापको मोल पूरा तिरियो।','Uhaanle bhannubhayo — siddhiyo. Haamro paapko mol puraa tiriyo.','He said: it is finished. The price of our sin was fully paid.','John 19:30']]},
{id:'jrisen',t:'He is risen',ne:'जीवित हुनुहुन्छ',art:FNE_ART.jrisen,
note:['सबै कुरा यही बिहानमा अडिन्छ। चिहान रित्तो भएकोले मृत्यु अब पर्खाल होइन, ढोका हो — र जीवित येशूले आज पनि मानिसहरूलाई नाम काढेर बोलाउनुहुन्छ।','Sabai kuraa yahi bihaanmaa adinchha. Chihaan ritto bhaekole mrityu aba parkhaal hoina, dhokaa ho — ra jeewit Yeshule aaja pani maanisharulaai naam kaadhera bolaunuhunchha.','Everything stands on this morning. Because the tomb is empty, death is no longer a wall but a door — and the risen Jesus still calls people by name.'],
paras:[
['आइतबार बिहान चिहान रित्तो थियो। येशू जीवित हुनुभएको थियो।','Aaitabaar bihaana chihaan ritto thiyo. Yeshu jeewit hunubhaeko thiyo.','On Sunday morning the tomb was empty. Jesus was alive.','Luke 24:1–8'],
['मरियम मग्दलिनी — येशूलाई पछ्याउने एउटी स्त्री — चिहान नजिक रोइरहेकी थिइन्। उनले उहाँलाई चिनिनन् — जबसम्म उहाँले एउटै शब्द भन्नुभयो — मरियम। आफ्नो नाम सुन्नेबित्तिकै उनले चिनिन्।','Mariyam Magdalini — Yeshulaai pachhyaaune euti stree — chihaan najik roirahekii thiin. Unle uhaanlaai chininan — jabasamma uhaanle eutai shabda bhannubhayo — Mariyam. Aaphno naam sunnebittikai unle chinin.','Mary Magdalene — a woman who had followed Jesus — stood weeping near the tomb. She did not recognize him, until he spoke a single word: Mary. The moment she heard her name, she knew.','John 20:14–16'],
['चेला थोमाले भने — नदेखी म विश्वास गर्दिनँ। येशू आउनुभयो र भन्नुभयो — मेरा हातहरू हेर, छोएर हेर। थोमाले भने — मेरा प्रभु, मेरा परमेश्वर!','Chelaa Thomaale bhane — nadekhi ma vishwaas gardinan. Yeshu aaunubhayo ra bhannubhayo — meraa haatharu hera, chhoera hera. Thomaale bhane — meraa Prabhu, meraa Parameshwar!','Thomas said: unless I see, I will not believe. Jesus came to him and said: look at my hands — touch and see. Thomas cried out: my Lord and my God!','John 20:24–29'],
['उहाँको मृत्यु र पुनरुत्थानद्वारा हामी परमेश्वरसँग मिलाइयौं, र मानिसलाई पकडमा राख्ने अन्धकारका शक्तिहरू पराजित भए। त्योभन्दा पनि ठूलो कुरा — अब परमेश्वर आफ्नो आत्माद्वारा हामीभित्रै बास गर्नुहुन्छ। उहाँलाई भेट्न अब मन्दिर जानुपर्दैन; उहाँका मानिसहरू नै उहाँको मन्दिर भएका छन्।','Uhaanko mrityu ra punarutthaandwaaraa haami Parameshwarsanga milaaiyaun, ra maanislaai pakadmaa raakhne andhakaarkaa shaktiharu paraajit bhae. Tyobhandaa pani thulo kuraa — aba Parameshwar aaphno aatmaadwaaraa haamibhitrai baas garnuhunchha. Uhaanlaai bhetna aba mandir jaanupardaina; uhaankaa maanisharu nai uhaanko mandir bhaekaa chhan.','Through his death and resurrection we were reconciled to God, and the dark powers that held humanity in their grip were defeated. And more than that — God now dwells within us by his Spirit. We no longer go to a temple to meet him; his people ARE his temple.','Colossians 2:15 · 1 Corinthians 3:16'],
['उहाँले चेलाहरूलाई भन्नुभयो — जाओ, सबै जातिहरूलाई मेरा चेला बनाओ। म सधैँ तिमीहरूसँग छु।','Uhaanle chelaaharulaai bhannubhayo — jaao, sabai jaatiharulaai meraa chelaa banaao. Ma sadhain timiharusanga chhu.','He told his followers: go, make disciples of all nations — and remember, I am with you always.','Matthew 28:18–20'],
['येशूको जीवन, मृत्यु र पुनरुत्थानले संसार बदल्यो — एक-एक व्यक्ति गर्दै। आज पनि उहाँ जीवित हुनुहुन्छ, र उहाँले तपाईंलाई बोलाउनुहुन्छ।','Yeshuko jeewan, mrityu ra punarutthaanle sansaar badalyo — ek-ek vyakti gardai. Aaja pani uhaan jeewit hunuhunchha, ra uhaanle tapaainlaai bolaunuhunchha.','The life, death and resurrection of Jesus changed the world — one person at a time. He is alive today — and he is calling you.','Revelation 3:20']]}
]}
]});
